{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy","id":1490481,"title":"Sex and the Technocracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-16T20:16:50-07:00","id":1490481,"title":"Sex and the Technocracy","content":"I don\u2019t have \u201cTechnocracy Reloaded,\u201d so I am asking this question here.<br /> <br /> What is the Unions position on sexuality in general? What rules does it have about the sex lives of its members? How often do they use sex as a weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T01:14:42-07:00","id":1490491,"title":"","content":"In the splat books they seem to say that the Void Engineers and the Progenitors are easy going on both sexual activity and sexuality. And we have the example of the Void Engineer transman who the Progenitors helped transition into what would look like a cisgendered male even nude. Plus, both groups canonically treat men and women as full equals.<br /> <br /> I think ItX is not sex positive. I don't think they necessarily treat women or LBGTQ+ people badly. Sex and the machine don't mesh.<br /> <br /> The NWO and the Syndicate probably see themselves as up to date, but they're both old boys networks and fairly petty. So, while they aren't officially bigots, in practical terms it works out that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T03:56:59-07:00","id":1490505,"title":"","content":"For all that the Technocracy tries to appear like an omnipresent force, it is a shadowy conspiracy which relies on influence and association far more than authority. Indeed, what authority it does impose on its members must be reserved for the things it thinks are most important (e.g. the Timetable). What that means is that most of the bigotry (and there are quite a few examples of bigotry in the Technocracy) are systemic, not foundational. They don't come from the top, they come from bigoted members and the top allows it to happen. <br /> <br /> In general, though, the Technocracy is going to be looser and more cavalier about sex and preference and identity than the Traditions. The Traditions (many of them, anyways) see sex as spiritually or metaphysically powerful and the Technocracy does not. The Traditions are much more likely to see meaning in sex and identity while the Technocracy is much more likely to see utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T05:33:03-07:00","id":1490507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490491#post1490491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the splat books they seem to say that the Void Engineers and the Progenitors are easy going on both sexual activity and sexuality. And we have the example of the Void Engineer transman who the Progenitors helped transition into what would look like a cisgendered male even nude. Plus, both groups canonically treat men and women as full equals.<br /> <br /> I think ItX is not sex positive. I don't think they necessarily treat women or LBGTQ+ people badly. Sex and the machine don't mesh.<br /> <br /> The NWO and the Syndicate probably see themselves as up to date, but they're both old boys networks and fairly petty. So, while they aren't officially bigots, in practical terms it works out that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't read the book and i mean no offense, but that sounds like a huge lot of glossing over of history of facts for the sake of making a more shiny &amp; cuddly take of the Technocracy and a version of the Ascension War where they are more balanced with the traditions and gray than the actual consortium of $#!+bags the organization actually was meant to be.<br /> <br /> Scientific theories have been wielded for a far from insignificant time - centuries in fact - as tools to impose prejudices, support the social mores of certain groups of interest and classes or other groups to challenge them: there's &quot;scientific&quot; racism, the view of homossexualism as a mental disability, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing#Homosexuality_and_indecency_conviction\" target=\"_blank\">to be treated through chemical procedures</a>, eletroshock and more depending on period, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phrenology#Application\" target=\"_blank\">phrenology</a> (that was far from fringe for most of 19th century), among a plethora of ideas and acts that would spring from them.<br /> <br /> And i find it quite hard to swallow that the Technocracy, as the personification of status quo (and a self-serving, corrupt, exploitative one to boot) that it is, was somehow oblivious or uninvolved with any of these things that run roughshod alongside &quot;the walk of progress&quot; and many times hand in hand with it.<br /> <br /> Admitedly, it doesn't have to be all about opression and institutional abuse of people - there are the works, life and legacy of Sigmund Freud, that has a number of nuances, polemics and complications that the academics and professionals following the science he began struggle with to this day, the ups &amp; downs of society's view on the subject of male or female masturbation, etc, but the subject is a very complex, convoluted and thorny one indeed with much sensitive stuff to discuss, highlight or touch upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-17-2022, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T07:23:36-07:00","id":1490513,"title":"","content":"Syndicate like whatever makes money and as they say, Sex sells. Hell I saw sex in the title and was like &quot;Oh, let's go here&quot;. Whether they're accepting of less-common positions or not probably depends entirely upon their target demographic. <br /> Progenitors will accept any biological challenge they see. <br /> NWO.. I can't imagine unity here. Some of them probably want to use conversion &quot;therapy&quot; with the mind sphere (which would be kinda interesting since the application of the mind sphere would probably get it to work, unlike conversion therapy IRL) while others will see the positives of acceptance. I'd estimate most don't really care that much and will just do whatever fulfills their political ambitions. <br /> <br /> ITX? On one hand, the flesh is to be detested. On the other: Sexbots and curious hypertech. <br /> <br /> <br /> Mages have a lot more power than ordinary people. I expect many of them to abuse it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T08:06:09-07:00","id":1490516,"title":"","content":"I see the Technocracy is largely in line with more modern viewpoints and/or those of the establishment. This means that the Technocracy would largely be (and ideologically support) permissive views of sexuality, tolerance of LGBT, birth control, alternative relationships and families, and the like. I think that Iteration X may be a bit of an exception in that they would see more open sexuality as a personal failing, though not really in any sort of traditional way.<br /> <br /> As for using sex as a weapon, I imagine that both the Syndicate and New World Order as making extensive use of sex. Pornography is a big business and I'm sure that the Syndicate has extensive influence in the sex industry, including control over content. The New World Order likely monitors the sex lives of allies and enemies alike and is able to use information they gain to put pressure on people. Much like how someone like Jeffrey Epstein (and whoever is affiliated with him) would be able to exert massive pressure over powerful people who engaged in elicit activity on his island. I imagine that the Technocracy has a number of similar individuals working for them who provide sexual services to powerful people in exchange for power and control. Depending on how dark we want our setting, we could get super dark with Syndicate controlled sex trafficking, organized crime, pedophile politicians, and related topics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T13:57:17-07:00","id":1490541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy#post1490481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t have \u201cTechnocracy Reloaded,\u201d so I am asking this question here.<br /> <br /> What is the Union's position on sexuality in general? What rules does it have about the sex lives of its members? How often do they use sex as a weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer: Most don't care as long as you don't make it a problem. Thing is, what constitutes a problem to the technocracy could be something as simple as trying to celebrate diversity. The modern technocratic union has finally understood that it needs to be flexible, but only to a point. The technocratic union is still very much an organization that puts order and uniformity as their priority.<br /> Here's how I imagine a conversation about the topic between a manager and an agent:<br /> So, you're gay/lesbian/trans/etc...? And? How about you go back to work instead of wasting the unions time? And that also goes for that pride day you suggested, demanding special attention is not mutual and will result in cognitive readjustment, am I clear? I don't care about your explanations about recognition or anything else, if you're not working for the timetable then you're working against it, now get out of my office.<br /> As a weapon, they use it the same as always: it's a commodity to sell, a way to get information or a tool to tempt your enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 08-18-2022, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T15:08:58-07:00","id":1490548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490507#post1490507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven't read the book and i mean no offense, but that sounds like a huge lot of glossing over of history of facts for the sake of making a more shiny &amp; cuddly take of the Technocracy and a version of the Ascension War where they are more balanced with the traditions and gray than the actual consortium of $#!+bags the organization actually was meant to be.<br /> <br /> Scientific theories have been wielded for a far from insignificant time - centuries in fact - as tools to impose prejudices, support the social mores of certain groups of interest and classes or other groups to challenge them: there's &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot; racism, the view of homossexualism as a mental disability, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing#Homosexuality_and_indecency_conviction &amp;quot;]to</a> be treated through chemical procedures[/URL], eletroshock and more depending on period, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phrenology#Application&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">phrenology</a> (that was far from fringe for most of 19th century), among a plethora of ideas and acts that would spring from them.<br /> <br /> And i find it quite hard to swallow that the Technocracy, as the personification of status quo (and a self-serving, corrupt, exploitative one to boot) that it is, was somehow oblivious or uninvolved with any of these things that run roughshod alongside &amp;quot;the walk of progress&amp;quot; and many times hand in hand with it.<br /> <br /> Admitedly, it doesn't have to be all about opression and institutional abuse of people - there are the works, life and legacy of Sigmund Freud, that has a number of nuances, polemics and complications that the academics and professionals following the science he began struggle with to this day, the ups &amp; downs of society's view on the subject of male or female masturbation, etc, but the subject is a very complex, convoluted and thorny one indeed with much sensitive stuff to discuss, highlight or touch upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The technocracy is the establishment. In the 1950's, they would condemn Alan Turing to be chemically castrated. Today, big multi-national corporations run ads with the pride flag. In China, they'll persecute homossexuality, in the West they'll promote it. In Saudi Arabia they'll execute homossexuals.<br /> <br /> To them this is absolutely irrelevant. Or, better saying, it's just simply another tool of control to be used for their convenience.<br /> <br /> As for the actions of their own agents, as long as it doesnt get in the way of their jobs they dont care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T17:59:32-07:00","id":1490568,"title":"","content":"I would suspect that the Progenitors would be one of the most &quot;progressive&quot; groups, in terms of sex/gender. In reshaping bodies, ideas like sex and gender become equally fluid. They also have ways (via cloning, IVF and other methods) that sex is no longer necessary under their paradigm for the continuation of the species. The sex drive is a natural part of all species, so I expect that most Progenitors would recognize and accept that. For them, sex as pleasure ends up being the focus rather than sex for procreation. This could end up getting pretty dark with some Progenitors creating groups of functional sex-slaves and whatnot. <br /> <br /> Iteration X is on the opposite extreme. I would expect that for younger members, things like cybernetic dildos, sex-bots and the like would be common jokes or things they work towards. As they become more machine than human, the sex drive begins to vanish with their flesh. For older members, sex simply becomes a necessary means to continue the species and sex without the goal of procreation becomes pointless. Surprisingly while you'd expect Iteration X to push for things like sex-robots and whatnot, the oldest (most machinelike) members would feel that sex beyond the singular goal of procreation is completely pointless. <br /> <br /> The Syndicate would view sex = money and that would probably be the extent of an overall design philosophy. As long as sex is providing money, either directly or indirectly (from new people being born) then it's all okay. Obviously the Syndicate would be big into prostitution, though I expect the Union would be split between the desire to legalize it and the desire to keep it illegal. Individual members might bring their own ideas on sex, and what forms of sex are acceptable or unacceptable, but overall I don't think you'd see anything resembling a consensus in the Syndicate beyond the idea that sex should be treated like any other commodity. <br /> <br /> New World Order would probably focus more on traditional CIS heterosexual marriage. Their primary focus would be more on the demographic aspect and they would be pushing for American-style nuclear families (as those are easier to maintain and deal with - parents are kept busy working, children spend time watching TV or playing video games or watching social media so it makes it easy to indoctrinate them, etc). Families that are deemed &quot;deviant&quot; (whether homosexual or large extended families) would be pushed against. A lot of their focus would be in propaganda (idealizing the traditional nuclear family) or in city planning (more suburbs forcing people to have cars, etc). <br /> <br /> I suspect the Void Engineers wouldn't care much at all. As long as it doesn't interfere with the mission then they'd have a fairly laissez faire attitude towards sex. I expect that there would be some members with the &quot;find alien races and fuck them&quot; mentality, but it probably would be seen as fairly deviant. I'd expect most recruits would be shown some videos of what could happen if they decided to put their penis in the alien monster. Some would inevitably ignore the advice and they might end up in a warning video for the next batch of recuits.<br /> <br /> Overall that would be the Union's personal opinions on sex within each Union. New World Order would generally control the Technocracy's position on sex outside of the Union, or at least it's the only one that has any real reason to care about what Sleepers do in regards to sex, and that would skew towards modern CIS focused traditional marriage with a focus on ensuring procreation and demographics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T05:30:28-07:00","id":1490599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490568#post1490568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Overall that would be the Union's personal opinions on sex within each Union. New World Order would generally control the Technocracy's position on sex outside of the Union, or at least it's the only one that has any real reason to care about what Sleepers do in regards to sex, and that would skew towards modern CIS focused traditional marriage with a focus on ensuring procreation and demographics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont agree with that. The purpose of mass education have ALWAYS been INDOCTRINATION.<br /> <br /> Mass public education began with Otto Von Bismarck (which in my opinion, if any real world personality would ever have been a techie, would've been him), and the purpose of it was to create &quot;patriotic&quot; (obedient) citizens to become good soldiers.<br /> <br /> The entire world followed suit, and to this day mass education still follows the same model all over the world.<br /> <br /> As such, every single nation-state in the world tries to remove the influence of parents in the education of children, so that those can be more easily indoctrinated by the God-State.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the &quot;traditional-family&quot; is NOT something that the secret Overlords of the world push for.<br /> <br /> And that becomes blatant in more authoritarian countries. In the USSR, North Korea, Cuba, China etc etc kids were/are incentivized to snitch their parents for example, and people were afraid of their own children (lets not forget that the USSR was the inspiration for the 1984 book, and that the &quot;Big Brother&quot; is the inspiration for the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> Therefore, the &quot;ideal&quot; model for the Union, in particular for the NWO, would be hedonistic sexual behavior that maximizes the procreation but that completely breaks down all family ties, leaving the State as the sole guardian of all children. Which is what Nazi Germany, USSR, China, Cuba, North Korea and all other totalitarian dictatorships of the proletarians tried to do with their populations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T05:40:48-07:00","id":1490600,"title":"","content":"Once new a player who refined a drug to make you experiance each others organisms while experiencing your own. Currently pending approval.<br /> <br /> mind 3 I think with entropy 2 to make sure you both peak at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-18-2022, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T06:17:01-07:00","id":1490603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490599#post1490599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont agree with that. The purpose of mass education have ALWAYS been INDOCTRINATION.<br /> <br /> Mass public education began with Otto Von Bismarck (which in my opinion, if any real world personality would ever have been a techie, would've been him), and the purpose of it was to create &quot;patriotic&quot; (obedient) citizens to become good soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth pointing out that the idea is much older. In the Republic, Plato advances the idea that pursuing an a just society requires separating children from their parents and raising them in a correct way. It's a common theme throughout history, if you can't convince adults that your ideal society is good, bypass them and raise the next generation as believers. It should be obvious I don't think much of the idea (at least when it involves separating children from their parents) and view it as a warning sign of tyranny.<br /> <br /> More generally, and more applicably to this thread, when a faction sees a disparity between humanity as it is and humanity as it should be they often start trying to correct things by attacking the bonds between people. The generous interpretation of this is that they are trying to stop social ties from reinforcing the societies mistakes, the ungenerous interpretation is that isolated people are easier to indoctrinate (see cults). Take your pick. It is not necessary for Mage that the Technocracy go down this path, but it is certainly believable that they would. It is further believable that one of the paths they might take is undermining the nuclear family or any deeper meanings of sexuality or sexual identity.<br /> <br /> It should also be <i>optional</i>, so that groups can customize to the needs of their game and the needs of the players at their table. This is a subject where things can go very wrong very quickly in more than one way. &quot;The Technocracy is full of repressive prudes who are trying to force a restrictive, cis-normative, and false nuclear family to box people in&quot; and &quot;The Technocracy is full of puppet masters trying to degrade human sexuality to better manipulate damaged people&quot; are both potentially alienating depending on the life experiences of the people playing the game.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't go down this rabbit hole in any of my games, and I certainly wouldn't without talking to the players first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-18-2022, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:05:00-07:00","id":1490613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490603#post1490603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is worth pointing out that the idea is much older. In the Republic, Plato advances the idea that pursuing an a just society requires separating children from their parents and raising them in a correct way. It's a common theme throughout history, if you can't convince adults that your ideal society is good, bypass them and raise the next generation as believers. It should be obvious I don't think much of the idea (at least when it involves separating children from their parents) and view it as a warning sign of tyranny.<br /> <br /> More generally, and more applicably to this thread, when a faction sees a disparity between humanity as it is and humanity as it should be they often start trying to correct things by attacking the bonds between people. The generous interpretation of this is that they are trying to stop social ties from reinforcing the societies mistakes, the ungenerous interpretation is that isolated people are easier to indoctrinate (see cults). Take your pick. It is not necessary for Mage that the Technocracy go down this path, but it is certainly believable that they would. It is further believable that one of the paths they might take is undermining the nuclear family or any deeper meanings of sexuality or sexual identity.<br /> <br /> It should also be <i>optional</i>, so that groups can customize to the needs of their game and the needs of the players at their table. This is a subject where things can go very wrong very quickly in more than one way. &amp;quot;The Technocracy is full of repressive prudes who are trying to force a restrictive, cis-normative, and false nuclear family to box people in&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;The Technocracy is full of puppet masters trying to degrade human sexuality to better manipulate damaged people&amp;quot; are both potentially alienating depending on the life experiences of the people playing the game.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't go down this rabbit hole in any of my games, and I certainly wouldn't without talking to the players first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldnt go down there either in my games. As a thought experiment of &quot;fictious realism&quot;, I believe they would be equally confortable doing BOTH, even at the same time, for different groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:10:03-07:00","id":1490614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490599#post1490599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such, every single nation-state in the world tries to remove the influence of parents in the education of children, so that those can be more easily indoctrinated by the God-State.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the &quot;traditional-family&quot; is NOT something that the secret Overlords of the world push for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I imagine that the &quot;traditional family&quot; has been in the sights of the Technocracy since at least the rise of the Prussian Model for public schools. Maybe longer. Traditional families are inherently conservative in that they allow values to be passed from parent to child and are resistant to outside influence. In fact, the idea of the nuclear family being the traditional family was likely a result of the Technocracy (and in the real world, influence of industrialists and authoritarian states) because it facilitated modern economic life and reduced the influence of the community/tribe/village is which is the traditional family in a broader sense.<br /> <br /> Now the nuclear family is remnant of the traditional family and it still has a lot of influence, though the Technocracy would want to undermine the influence of the nuclear family and greater promiscuity (and generally more modern sexual mores) would likely be a method. With higher levels of divorce and/or single mothers, the more parents are going to want or even need outside help, and thus outside influence, to raise their children. The less influence parents have, then the more influence that school and media have over children, which is good for the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the eventual goal would be Brave New World: parenthood has been eliminated and all children are raised by the state. The breakdown of traditional sexual morality, including monogamy and the nuclear family, could facilitate that transition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:56:49-07:00","id":1490619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490614#post1490614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. I imagine that the &amp;quot;traditional family&amp;quot; has been in the sights of the Technocracy since at least the rise of the Prussian Model for public schools. Maybe longer. Traditional families are inherently conservative in that they allow values to be passed from parent to child and are resistant to outside influence. In fact, the idea of the nuclear family being the traditional family was likely a result of the Technocracy (and in the real world, influence of industrialists and authoritarian states) because it facilitated modern economic life and reduced the influence of the community/tribe/village is which is the traditional family in a broader sense.<br /> <br /> Now the nuclear family is remnant of the traditional family and it still has a lot of influence, though the Technocracy would want to undermine the influence of the nuclear family and greater promiscuity (and generally more modern sexual mores) would likely be a method. With higher levels of divorce and/or single mothers, the more parents are going to want or even need outside help, and thus outside influence, to raise their children. The less influence parents have, then the more influence that school and media have over children, which is good for the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the eventual goal would be Brave New World: parenthood has been eliminated and all children are raised by the state. The breakdown of traditional sexual morality, including monogamy and the nuclear family, could facilitate that transition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;traditional&quot; traditional family is exactly what you said, clans, tribes or villages. The &quot;traditional&quot; family of today - parents and children - however was &quot;invented&quot; long before the industrials. It was a medieval christian creation, thus it has been established in Europe for centuries, and yes, it became more of a norm outside of Europe due to the spread of the industrial revolution and the spread of urbanization throghout the globe.<br /> <br /> Be it as it may, the Prussian model spread all over the globe, and is adopted even by non western nations, because it gives power to the State - and the Technocracy is the artistic representation of the tyranny of the State, the embodiment of government opression over individuals.<br /> <br /> Yes, the inspirational sources for the idea of the Union are the dystopian novels, mostly 1984 and Brave New World, with a small dose of humor from the Men in Black movies, mixed with transhumanist ideologies and conspiracy theories (in special about the modern Illuminati conspiracy theories).<br /> <br /> So yes, the idea behind the Technocracy relies entirely into bringing up a dystopian &quot;paradise&quot; of total control and absolute centralization of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T09:09:49-07:00","id":1490620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490619#post1490619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;traditional&quot; traditional family is exactly what you said, clans, tribes or villages. The &quot;traditional&quot; family of today - parents and children - however was &quot;invented&quot; long before the industrials. It was a medieval christian creation, thus it has been established in Europe for centuries, and yes, it became more of a norm outside of Europe due to the spread of the industrial revolution and the spread of urbanization throghout the globe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I didn't mean to suggest that the nuclear family only arose with the industrial revolution. I'd say that the monogamous family (husband, wife, kids) has been a major component of the family going back through pre-history, but that the village and it's influence collapsed with modernity and the nuclear family is the remnant that survived.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T09:27:46-07:00","id":1490623,"title":"","content":"The christian family also included primes, grandparents (if alive)...and all the other relationships that would constitute what we would call today&quot;familiars&quot;, that lived together or relatively close. As said in my langauge &quot;la casa grande&quot; (or, &quot;the family house&quot;?, I don't know how to translate the concept) was the status quo until very recently (and in some places still is).<br /> <br /> There was a huge influence of the Industiralized era <i>even in Europe, </i> trough many factors, like the &quot;movement to the to the city&quot; or the ease of travel, that reduced the size of the family considerably. The idea that children need to leave the house of their parents and form &quot;their own&quot; nuclear family, which I think strongly shapes our idea of what a family looks today, it's not that old - at least talking from my experience with family customs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-18-2022, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T12:18:44-07:00","id":1490638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490623#post1490623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The christian family also included primes, grandparents (if alive)...and all the other relationships that would constitute what we would call today&amp;quot;familiars&amp;quot;, that lived together or relatively close. As said in my langauge &amp;quot;la casa grande&amp;quot; (or, &amp;quot;the family house&amp;quot;?, I don't know how to translate the concept) was the status quo until very recently (and in some places still is).<br /> <br /> There was a huge influence of the Industiralized era <i>even in Europe, </i> trough many factors, like the &amp;quot;movement to the to the city&amp;quot; or the ease of travel, that reduced the size of the family considerably. The idea that children need to leave the house of their parents and form &amp;quot;their own&amp;quot; nuclear family, which I think strongly shapes our idea of what a family looks today, it's not that old - at least talking from my experience with family customs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;La Casa Grande&quot; means &quot;The Big House&quot;. Yes, the &quot;traditional family&quot; initially was the clan. Then it became what today we would consider &quot;extended family&quot;. As you explained, cousins, uncles and aunts and so forth. That was a change brought by christianity. And with industrialization and particularly urbanization, that became even further reduced to the nucleous of parents and children.<br /> <br /> I dont think that the changes due to urbanization were pushed by the industrial elites, but rather a consequence of the changes brought to lifestyle of the masses, however it could well be that for the Mage games, this could well be something that were actively pushed by the Union as a way to push for control","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T16:01:32-07:00","id":1490659,"title":"","content":"The sex instinct will be eradicated. Procreation will be an annual formality like the renewal of a ration card. We shall abolish the orgasm. Our neurologists are at work upon it now.<br /> \u2013 George Orwell<br /> (1984. Part 3, Chapter 3. O\u2019Brien during Winston\u2019s re-education by the Thought Police. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-18-2022, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T08:58:27-07:00","id":1490715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490659#post1490659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sex instinct will be eradicated. Procreation will be an annual formality like the renewal of a ration card. We shall abolish the orgasm. Our neurologists are at work upon it now.<br /> \u2013 George Orwell<br /> (1984. Part 3, Chapter 3. O\u2019Brien during Winston\u2019s re-education by the Thought Police. )</div> </div> </div> </div>I find any works of horror, be it movies or books, to be rather silly. Even Call of Cthulhu never caused in me any feelings except a sort of amazed curiosity.<br /> <br /> But the 1984 book has left me absolutely terrorized. I can confidently say that such a scenario is the only thing that petrifies me. I dont fear death at all, but the insane dystopia of 1984 horrifies me.<br /> <br /> If I believed in Hell, this is what it would be, not lakes of fire but the Big Brother watching every single one of my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Thou honestly, I dont know which one is worse, if 1984 or Brave New World. In both however, the obliteration of family ties is essential for the total control, so that's something we can agree. For the State (represented by the Technocratic Union) to control the individuals, all ties between individuals must be broken, so that people are fully bind into the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T22:07:07-07:00","id":1490761,"title":"","content":"With the right spheres, you could have sex only once and stay in the afterglow for the rest of your life. Your body would be maintained in the chemical state that follows sex. This would appeal to the Technocracy, because it reduces the need to go out in search of a partner and the time it takes to get in the mood, do the deed and get clean after. I still think a lot of sex happens in Constructs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T01:30:54-07:00","id":1490771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490761#post1490761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the right spheres, you could have sex only once and stay in the afterglow for the rest of your life. Your body would be maintained in the chemical state that follows sex. This would appeal to the Technocracy, because it reduces the need to go out in search of a partner and the time it takes to get in the mood, do the deed and get clean after. I still think a lot of sex happens in Constructs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mind Sphere can be used to replace sex alltogheter. <br /> <br /> Sex can be removed and induced by the Union in different cases, with both approaches being used. It can serve as a bounding tool for an amalgam for instance, to increase group loyalty and cohesion (yeah, that means orgies). And it can also be removed for others, to remove any connections between individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T15:43:54-07:00","id":1490816,"title":"","content":"So, my copy of Technocracy Reloaded spent quite a while in limbo and the physical one still isn't with me as I sent it to a buddy rather then to myself. This thread made me take a look at the pdf. There is actually quite a bit of text in the book about what the Technocracy thinks of sex, relationships and gender identity:<ul><li>Technocracy realised they had an issue with toxic masculinity from 1900s to1980s</li> <li>Chauvinism and machismo were seen as unproductive and wasteful and efforts were made to correct it</li> <li>No restrictions on sexual preferences or gender identity</li> <li>Only effective operatives are the ones who are comfortable with their identity, therefore technocracy offers hypertech gender-affirmation surgery to help their members with issues</li> <li>The former is actually seen as decadent and corrupt by certain Traditions</li> <li>Sexual preference stigmas are officially forbidden in the Technocracy</li> <li>There may be certain situations where the Technocracy restricts who you can be with (cowerkers, special mission types)</li> <li>Birth control and STD prevention/control for all</li> <li>Having children is limited by requiring a certain rank in the Technocracy</li> <li>Citizens have no limitations on having kids, meaning that low level mages are the ones most impacted by this</li> <li>All the above stuff - treatment, birth control and gender-reaffirming procedures - are available to the Citizens! &quot;Happy healthy, satisfied workforce tends to be an extremely loyal workforce&quot;</li> <li>Stigma and harsh punishments for any form of sexual violence</li> <li>Children are a priority and anyone in Technocracy is expected to educate and help with them</li> <li>Cannot date direct superiors or direct subordinates, harsh consequences</li> <li>If the other side is eligible, relationship status needs to be reported, and no sex before paperwork</li> <li>Sex =/= Relationship</li> <li>Sex and polyamoury are quite common, especially in Iteration X and NWO</li> <li>So is asexuality - be it due to being processed, traumatized or not built for it, asexual people feel especially comfortable here</li> <li>Syndicate is sex crazed and tends to ignore rules about relationships (except rape), love of abusing power dynamics,sex is a weapon and domination is a mark of success, this makes other conventions wary of them</li> <li>Progenitors have a almost creepy fascination with the mechanics of procreation</li> <li>The Void Engineers are both geeky cosmonauts and the horniest technocrats alive (also sex with extradimensional beings can make men pregnant)</li> <li>Marriage is only allowed for high rank technocrats with high loyalty, no boundaries on gender, sexual identity or number of people you are married to</li> <li>You get to work with the people you are married to and usually get joint assignments</li> <li>Joint quarters and</li> <li>Married people get licenses for kids more easily, also parental leave</li> <li>Partnership is the &quot;simple&quot; variant of Marriage without the bureacracy, less concessions from Technocracy</li> <li>Divorce is handled by giving the sides involved separate quarters and a mediator to establish if there is any damage to the Technocracy, relationship counseling is offered if it can help, if not communal belongings are shared equally unless there are infractions or abuse, Children become wards of the Union (many Technocrats prefer to stay married for this reason)</li> </ul><br /> ... Yes, THAT IS A LOT OF WORDCOUNT if this is just a summary. Check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T17:49:57-07:00","id":1490829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490816#post1490816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my copy of Technocracy Reloaded spent quite a while in limbo and the physical one still isn't with me as I sent it to a buddy rather then to myself. This thread made me take a look at the pdf. There is actually quite a bit of text in the book about what the Technocracy thinks of sex, relationships and gender identity:<ul><li>Technocracy realised they had an issue with toxic masculinity from 1900s to1980s</li> <li>Chauvinism and machismo were seen as unproductive and wasteful and efforts were made to correct it</li> <li>No restrictions on sexual preferences or gender identity</li> <li>Only effective operatives are the ones who are comfortable with their identity, therefore technocracy offers hypertech gender-affirmation surgery to help their members with issues</li> <li>The former is actually seen as decadent and corrupt by certain Traditions</li> <li>Sexual preference stigmas are officially forbidden in the Technocracy</li> <li>There may be certain situations where the Technocracy restricts who you can be with (cowerkers, special mission types)</li> <li>Birth control and STD prevention/control for all</li> <li>Having children is limited by requiring a certain rank in the Technocracy</li> <li>Citizens have no limitations on having kids, meaning that low level mages are the ones most impacted by this</li> <li>All the above stuff - treatment, birth control and gender-reaffirming procedures - are available to the Citizens! &amp;quot;Happy healthy, satisfied workforce tends to be an extremely loyal workforce&amp;quot;</li> <li>Stigma and harsh punishments for any form of sexual violence</li> <li>Children are a priority and anyone in Technocracy is expected to educate and help with them</li> <li>Cannot date direct superiors or direct subordinates, harsh consequences</li> <li>If the other side is eligible, relationship status needs to be reported, and no sex before paperwork</li> <li>Sex =/= Relationship</li> <li>Sex and polyamoury are quite common, especially in Iteration X and NWO</li> <li>So is asexuality - be it due to being processed, traumatized or not built for it, asexual people feel especially comfortable here</li> <li>Syndicate is sex crazed and tends to ignore rules about relationships (except rape), love of abusing power dynamics,sex is a weapon and domination is a mark of success, this makes other conventions wary of them</li> <li>Progenitors have a almost creepy fascination with the mechanics of procreation</li> <li>The Void Engineers are both geeky cosmonauts and the horniest technocrats alive (also sex with extradimensional beings can make men pregnant)</li> <li>Marriage is only allowed for high rank technocrats with high loyalty, no boundaries on gender, sexual identity or number of people you are married to</li> <li>You get to work with the people you are married to and usually get joint assignments</li> <li>Joint quarters and</li> <li>Married people get licenses for kids more easily, also parental leave</li> <li>Partnership is the &amp;quot;simple&amp;quot; variant of Marriage without the bureacracy, less concessions from Technocracy</li> <li>Divorce is handled by giving the sides involved separate quarters and a mediator to establish if there is any damage to the Technocracy, relationship counseling is offered if it can help, if not communal belongings are shared equally unless there are infractions or abuse, Children become wards of the Union (many Technocrats prefer to stay married for this reason)</li> </ul><br /> ... Yes, THAT IS A LOT OF WORDCOUNT if this is just a summary. Check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some pretty progressive fascists if I may say hahaha.<br /> <br /> I DO however believe that to be realitisc for the Techies as they're envisoned.<br /> <br /> Also, incredible twist there with the <b><i>Traditions</i></b> being, you know, traditional... And thus being the real &quot;evil&quot; and &quot;depicable&quot; &quot;alt-right&quot; &quot;nutjobs&quot; (not to mention how they are literally anti &quot;science&quot;).<br /> <br /> Of course, we should expect all of that nuance to be absolutely nuked away on M5 for the sake of current affairs real world politics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T17:53:30-07:00","id":1490830,"title":"","content":"You haven't seen Lore of the Traditions yet, have you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T11:42:24-07:00","id":1490908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490830#post1490830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't seen Lore of the Traditions yet, have you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please continue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T13:06:21-07:00","id":1490916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490830#post1490830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't seen Lore of the Traditions yet, have you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please continue<br /> <br /> Edit: sorry, accidental double post. I dont know how to delete it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-21-2022, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T13:47:35-07:00","id":1490924,"title":"","content":"There is no way to delete. <br /> <br /> Lore of the Traditions is an upcoming supplement for Mage that has as its basis the idea that each Tradition has seen the error of its ways and has attempted to correct them. This means that anything that might smack of the Traditions being <i>&quot;evil&quot; and &quot;depicable&quot; &quot;alt-right&quot; &quot;nutjobs&quot; (not to mention how they are literally anti &quot;science&quot;)</i> has been purged to the extent that it's possible to do so. <br /> <br /> (On the anti-science thing, the Traditions haven't been \u201canti-science\u201d for a long time; most of them have been \u201calternative to science\u201d to the extent that they've confronted the issue at all, and have mainly been \u201canti-technocracy\u201d; and in Lore of the Traditions, the Society of Ether flat out accuses the <i>Technocracy</i> of being anti-science.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T15:25:15-07:00","id":1490938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490924#post1490924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore of the Traditions is an upcoming supplement for Mage that has as its basis the idea that each Tradition has seen the error of its ways and has attempted to correct them. This means that anything that might smack of the Traditions being <i>&quot;evil&quot; and &quot;depicable&quot; &quot;alt-right&quot; &quot;nutjobs&quot; (not to mention how they are literally anti &quot;science&quot;)</i> has been purged to the extent that it's possible to do so.<br /> <br /> (On the anti-science thing, the Traditions haven't been \u201canti-science\u201d for a long time; most of them have been \u201calternative to science\u201d to the extent that they've confronted the issue at all, and have mainly been \u201canti-technocracy\u201d; and in Lore of the Traditions, the Society of Ether flat out accuses the <i>Technocracy</i> of being anti-science.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... not sure that's the way to go with this, as one of the problems of the Traditions is that they're fixated on their ideas for better or for worse. They probably came into this from the whole anti-science post-truth conversation in America, but the Traditions should have their warts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T16:53:42-07:00","id":1490951,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the Lore of the Traditions is a book I won\u2019t be picking up. If that is what the book will be like, then it seems like the writers don\u2019t understand Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T09:57:37-07:00","id":1491007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1490924#post1490924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no way to delete. <br /> <br /> Lore of the Traditions is an upcoming supplement for Mage that has as its basis the idea that each Tradition has seen the error of its ways and has attempted to correct them. This means that anything that might smack of the Traditions being <i>&amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;depicable&amp;quot; &amp;quot;alt-right&amp;quot; &amp;quot;nutjobs&amp;quot; (not to mention how they are literally anti &amp;quot;science&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i> has been purged to the extent that it's possible to do so. <br /> <br /> (On the anti-science thing, the Traditions haven't been \u201canti-science\u201d for a long time; most of them have been \u201calternative to science\u201d to the extent that they've confronted the issue at all, and have mainly been \u201canti-technocracy\u201d; and in Lore of the Traditions, the Society of Ether flat out accuses the <i>Technocracy</i> of being anti-science.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, we cant let nuance and actual good writting and an engaging story get in the way of modern real life politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T10:34:48-07:00","id":1491009,"title":"","content":"I read Technocracy Reloaded and I loved all the stuff in there about sex and the Technocracy. Really progressive. I\u2019m looking forward to seeing how the Traditions view sex and sexual stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T19:52:29-07:00","id":1491071,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy absolutely should be progressive. The Traditions, on the other hand, are literally called \u201cthe Traditions\u201d and are meant to represent those ideologies which were defeated by progress.<br /> <br /> They actually are anti-science, because in M:tA prayers or spells aren\u2019t inherently worse ways to fight disease than vaccines are. Of course, in real life, real doctors are better than witch doctors, but we have to divorce our real life beliefs and knowledge from M:tA for the setting to make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T21:20:29-07:00","id":1491075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491071#post1491071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy absolutely should be progressive. The Traditions, on the other hand, are literally called \u201cthe Traditions\u201d and are meant to represent those ideologies which were defeated by progress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that would be the Crafts. The Traditions <i>do</i> frequently Practice Magick in ways that the Technocracy has \u201cdebunked\u201d; but that's not what they're about. They're about cooperation and mingling; the central tenet that unites the traditions is the belief that they're all on a fundamental level doing the same thing. <br /> <br /> That's why Traditional Chantries are usually cross-Tradition, with Choristers, Verbenae, Etherites, Hermetics, etc. working side by side as colleagues, often even working Effects together that blend their individual approaches to Magick to produce results that none of them could achieve on their own. <br /> <br /> Heck, the ways of Magick in the Traditions don't form nine discrete points; they form a continuum. Pick two Traditions, and you'll find mages who practice a merger of their beliefs. And you'll find practitioners of these \u201chybrid styles\u201d in both Traditions. And note again that one of those Traditions is the Etherites, meaning that those \u201cmixed magic\u201d mages include technomancers. Which brings us to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491071#post1491071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They actually are anti-science, because in M:tA prayers or spells aren\u2019t inherently worse ways to fight disease than vaccines are. Of course, in real life, real doctors are better than witch doctors, but we have to divorce our real life beliefs and knowledge from M:tA for the setting to make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not <i>anti-</i>science; that implies that they don't accept science as a valid way of doing things. And the Etherites among them wouldn't stand for that. They don't <i>reject</i> science. They're <i>alt-</i>science: they believe that their ways are <i>just as valid</i> as the science pushed by the Technocracy. Their biggest gripe with the Technocracy is its \u201cOne Right Way\u201d mentality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-23-2022, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T15:21:25-07:00","id":1491130,"title":"","content":"I am waiting on Lore of the Traditions to make my judgement. But my issue with the posts above about the Tehnocracy is that it feels too forgiving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T15:49:30-07:00","id":1491134,"title":"","content":"Please clarify: what do you mean by \u201cit\u201d in \u201cit feels too forgiving\u201d? The Technocracy feels too forgiving? The comments about the Technocracy feel too forgiving? Something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:48:15-07:00","id":1491143,"title":"","content":"Yes. I meant the position on sex and sexuality feels too humane for the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:57:20-07:00","id":1491146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491071#post1491071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Technocracy absolutely should be progressive.</b> The Traditions, on the other hand, are literally called \u201cthe Traditions\u201d and are <b>meant to represent those ideologies which were defeated by progress.</b><br /> <br /> They actually are anti-science, because in M:tA prayers or spells aren\u2019t inherently worse ways to fight disease than vaccines are. Of course, in real life, real doctors are better than witch doctors, but we have to divorce our real life beliefs and knowledge from M:tA for the setting to make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was nothing inherently progressive about them turning technology into the dominant paradigm of reality in human consciousness over the magic used by the traditions. So far as the setting is concerned technology is just a kind of magic that happened to get super popular and whose adherents were great at convincing people other forms of magic don't actually work (which via settings mechanics makes it to where they actually do start working less well). The fact that the traditions are multiple different kinds of magic users who work together and acknowledge that other means of doing magic are valid makes them much more 'progressive' in the political sense you are thinking of then the Technocracy and their persecution of anyone who does magic differently from them. Even the proudest most stiff necked superiority complex having members of the Order of Hermes (the go to faction amongst the traditions for arrogance) don't think people should be banned from doing non-hermetic magic on pain of death like has happened with the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> You seem to have it backwards on which side is actively trying to wipe the other out of existence. It is the technocracy that is trying to wipe out any other kind of magic then their own 'hyper science' from existence as being invalid. The traditions are mostly just fighting to stay alive and viable in the face of a concentrated campaign to erase them from existence by a bunch of fascists that decided their magic has no right to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-23-2022, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T04:47:57-07:00","id":1491182,"title":"","content":"No, the Technocracy are the progressive ones. The idea that all technology is just magic that got popular is some very extreme hubris. If we're talking vacuum tubes and semi conductors, maybe, but near everything else is just creative use of basic things like the wheel or fire. But the order of reason is correct. If it were up to the Traditions (tech guys excluded) most would lord over a primitive world and push their inane beliefs on the masses for the pure furtherment of the mage's power. Technology challenges a Mage's power. The Order of Reason puts people first before their magic. Tech is built for the advancement of humanity and the OoR builds upon this. The Technocracy are better off than most but they're not lords and they're not bothered by ordinary people having a realistic means to challenge them because they're not ruling through fear. Now, you might argue that inadvertently they might make the world worse: The industrial revolution and our future fully-automated police state certainly have disadvantages compared to living hunter-gatherer or within an ancient empire, but the end state will be better. The Technocracy is the faction of universal progress. The Traditions are dangerous people set in outdated ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T05:46:39-07:00","id":1491189,"title":"","content":"That's definitely how the Technocracy sees it, yes. And in my preferred take on the Mage setting (where Enlightened Science is built on Earthly Foundations, which is essentially what your comment about \u201cthe creative use of the wheel or fire\u201d is all about), they're not <i>wrong</i>. <br /> <br /> But they're also not right. While I'll agree that the Traditions at their worst are more interested in the pursuit of Ascension than they are about the well-being of the Sleepers, they're <i>not</i> \u201cset in outdated ways\u201d: what the Traditions do <i>works</i>. Sure, it tends to be more Paradox-prone than Enlightened Science, which only has to contend with the Consensus making something Vulgar, as opposed to having to contend with <i>both</i> the Consensus <i>and</i> Earthly Foundations; but it still works. <br /> <br /> And just as importantly, \u201cthe Order of Reason puts people first before their magic\u201d, and \u201cthey're not lords and they're not bothered by ordinary people having a realistic means to challenge them because they're not ruling through fear\u201d are just plain <i>false</i>. There <i>were</i> Enlightened Scientists once upon a time who thought like that; they were called the Craftsmasons; and while they helped create the Order of Reason with that goal in mind, from the earliest days, they spent much of their time fighting the tendency of their fellow Daedeleans to ignore or lord over the Masses. (And to the extent that the Technocracy doesn't rule through fear, it's usually because they have more subtle and effective ways to rule.)<br /> <br /> In the 1600s, the Craftsmasons were destroyed by the Order of Reason, precisely because the other Conventions rejected what they stood for. By the 1800s, the Order of Reason was rapidly transforming into the Technocracy \u2014 an apt term for them which refers to \u201crule by technical elites\u201d. <br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> still some in the Union who hold to the ideals of the Craftsmasons; but they're a minority. Of the majority, the most benign are the ones who ignore the Masses and spend all of their time seeking to advance Enlightened Science \u2014 ironically, the very thing you accuse the Traditions of doing. The more problematic ones are <i>moral busybodies</i> who actively seek to interfere in the lives of the Masses, \u201cfor their own good\u201d; they're convinced that they know better than the Masses what's good for them.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Of all tyrannies, a tyranny sincerely exercised for the good of its victims may be the most oppressive. It would be better to live under robber barons than under omnipotent moral busybodies. The robber baron's cruelty may sometimes sleep, his cupidity may at some point be satiated; but those who torment us for our own good will torment us without end for they do so with the approval of their own conscience. They may be more likely to go to Heaven yet at the same time likelier to make a Hell of earth. This very kindness stings with intolerable insult. To be &quot;cured&quot; against one's will and cured of states which we may not regard as disease is to be put on a level of those who have not yet reached the age of reason or those who never will; to be classed with infants, imbeciles, and domestic animals.<br /> <br /> \u2014C.S. Lewis</div><i>This</i> is the great flaw of the Technocratic Union: a benevolent tyranny that ends up treating the people it claims to help as if they were subhuman. <br /> <br /> I think this is where <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> is coming from: seeing the Technocracy mostly portrayed as \u201cyour sex life is your business and not ours\u201d runs directly counter to the Union's tendency to stick its collective nose into everyone's business. I <i>can</i> see that as the official position of the Void Engineers; they tend to have bigger concerns to occupy them than trying to regulate who sleeps with whom. But the other Conventions? Not so much. Each likely has an overall view on sex; and those views are almost certainly <i>not</i> \u201cif it's not harming anyone, do as you will\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-24-2022, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T06:12:45-07:00","id":1491191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491143#post1491143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I meant the position on sex and sexuality feels too humane for the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well some of it is quite incoherent if you dig into it. For instance, the Technocracy's motivations towards treating gender dysphoria are purely practical, not moral (it's about effectiveness, not identity), so their method is going to be based on expedience. Well, given that four of the five Conventions are quite comfortable psychologically conditioning their members, it is much more believable that the Technocracy would use Mind rather than Life to help operators &quot;be comfortable with their identity.&quot; <br /> <br /> Now that obviously wasn't going to happen; the writers/paradox/etc. would not want to send that message. The Technocracy, though, wouldn't care if it sent that message. It doesn't mind using Mind to change how people think about themselves. Room 101 establishes that quite well.<br /> <br /> That said, there's no particular reason they would avoid using Life rather than Mind, it just isn't as believable.<br /> <br /> Setting inconsistencies aside, Technocracy's policies towards sex and sexual identity likely come from one of two sources:<br /> <br /> 1) They are unintentional outgrowths of the belief that sex and sexual identity have no meaning beyond the physical and psychological (both of which the Technocracy can control)<br /> <br /> 2) They are intentional policy decisions because sex and sexual identity shouldn't have a meaning beyond the physical and psychological.(both of which the Technocracy use to control)<br /> <br /> So as to your point about humanity, I would say that if their policy is humane it is at least inhumanely humane. It is born of uncaring utility rather than a strong moral stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T06:23:54-07:00","id":1491192,"title":"","content":"The NWO would be inclined to use Mind, to adjust it to match the biology; the Progenitors would be more inclined to use Life, to adjust the biology to match the psychology; Iteration X would be more inclined to use conjunctional Life and Matter to take the biology out of the issue entirely; and the Syndicate would be more inclined to use Prime to monetize the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T08:38:06-07:00","id":1491196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491146#post1491146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was nothing inherently progressive about them turning technology into the dominant paradigm of reality in human consciousness over the magic used by the traditions. So far as the setting is concerned technology is just a kind of magic that happened to get super popular and whose adherents were great at convincing people other forms of magic don't actually work (which via settings mechanics makes it to where they actually do start working less well). The fact that the traditions are multiple different kinds of magic users who work together and acknowledge that other means of doing magic are valid makes them much more 'progressive' in the political sense you are thinking of then the Technocracy and their persecution of anyone who does magic differently from them. Even the proudest most stiff necked superiority complex having members of the Order of Hermes (the go to faction amongst the traditions for arrogance) don't think people should be banned from doing non-hermetic magic on pain of death like has happened with the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> You seem to have it backwards on which side is actively trying to wipe the other out of existence. It is the technocracy that is trying to wipe out any other kind of magic then their own 'hyper science' from existence as being invalid. The traditions are mostly just fighting to stay alive and viable in the face of a concentrated campaign to erase them from existence by a bunch of fascists that decided their magic has no right to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to conflate &quot;progressivism&quot; with &quot;being nice&quot;. And then you throw in a &quot;fascists&quot; as a way to justify it, to justapose progressivism with fascism and to try to make it look like those are polar opposites, when in fact they are not.<br /> <br /> Every single revolutionaire is a progressive, and every progressive is at least a bit revolutionaire. The idea is, after all, to &quot;push society foward&quot;, going away with the old and introducing the new.<br /> <br /> Now, a healthy society will have a healthy balance between keeping their traditions and changing and adapting. Societies too stifled with conservatism becomes suffocated and unable to change, and will be buried by an ever changing world. That's what happened to the chinese empire for example.<br /> <br /> Societies too hellbent on change however will simply consume themselves into a revolutionare frenzy. And oh boy, the &quot;progressives&quot; when such thing happens are much much worse than Mussolini - and even worse than Hitler sometimes. That's what happened with the French Revolution and their &quot;Terror&quot;, with hundreds of thousands beheaded in the name of &quot;progress&quot;. That's what happened in the USSR and China with dozens of MILLIONS of deaths.<br /> <br /> Progressives can and often are absolutely fascists. One thing does NOT exclude the other at all.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Techbocracy is beyond any doubt, both Progressive AND Fascist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T09:01:30-07:00","id":1491197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491191#post1491191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well some of it is quite incoherent if you dig into it. For instance, the Technocracy's motivations towards treating gender dysphoria are purely practical, not moral (it's about effectiveness, not identity), so their method is going to be based on expedience. Well, given that four of the five Conventions are quite comfortable psychologically conditioning their members, it is much more believable that the Technocracy would use Mind rather than Life to help operators &amp;quot;be comfortable with their identity.&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> Now that obviously wasn't going to happen; the writers/paradox/etc. would not want to send that message. The Technocracy, though, wouldn't care if it sent that message. It doesn't mind using Mind to change how people think about themselves. Room 101 establishes that quite well.<br /> <br /> That said, there's no particular reason they would avoid using Life rather than Mind, it just isn't as believable.<br /> <br /> Setting inconsistencies aside, Technocracy's policies towards sex and sexual identity likely come from one of two sources:<br /> <br /> 1) They are unintentional outgrowths of the belief that sex and sexual identity have no meaning beyond the physical and psychological (both of which the Technocracy can control)<br /> <br /> 2) They are intentional policy decisions because sex and sexual identity shouldn't have a meaning beyond the physical and psychological.(both of which the Technocracy use to control)<br /> <br /> So as to your point about humanity, I would say that if their policy is humane it is at least inhumanely humane. It is born of uncaring utility rather than a strong moral stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing sex with a Life effect is much harder than changing somebody's sexual identity using Mind. So, for practical terms, I do believe that the Techies would be much more likely to simply brainwash an agent, unless this is done for the sake of the moral on the ranks; being constantly on the lookout for your superiors to send you to Room 101 is not the best HR way to keep your agents motivated. It's also a good internal PR - &quot;we take care of our own!&quot;.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think that such an organization in real life would just simply become a sort of monstruous Hivemind. Why leaving your agents with any individuality at all? Why not just simply brainwashing EVERYBODY if you're capable of? Turning every single Technocrat into basically brainwashed drones, obediently following Control's every commands without questions - such is the dangers of transhumanism ideas for example. If humanity collectively in the future connects all of their brains to the &quot;internet&quot;, what stop us from turning into a massive Hivemind, where our individualities are absolutely crushed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T09:20:24-07:00","id":1491199,"title":"","content":"A hive mind technocracy would fail. In part, because there's not (yet?) The ability to maintain a network of agents in a way that cannot be disrupted. At least for now, the technocracy needs individual agents to be individuals with agency in order to be able to react to the unexpected. That said, the hive mind idea is something that upper management, at least, would be looking into. You see it in threat null, for example; where Transhumanity is a hive mind. But then, the concept behind threat null is that it is the technocracy taken closer to its logical extreme \u2014 and implementation of the 1e concept of the technocracy, where the agents are monsters that have been scrubbed of their humanity. The actual technocracy isn't that far gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:07:13-07:00","id":1491207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491182#post1491182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Technocracy are the progressive ones. The idea that all technology is just magic that got popular is some very extreme hubris. If we're talking vacuum tubes and semi conductors, maybe, but near everything else is just creative use of basic things like the wheel or fire. But the order of reason is correct. If it were up to the Traditions (tech guys excluded) most would lord over a primitive world and push their inane beliefs on the masses for the pure furtherment of the mage's power. Technology challenges a Mage's power. The Order of Reason puts people first before their magic. Tech is built for the advancement of humanity and the OoR builds upon this. The Technocracy are better off than most but they're not lords and they're not bothered by ordinary people having a realistic means to challenge them because they're not ruling through fear. Now, you might argue that inadvertently they might make the world worse: The industrial revolution and our future fully-automated police state certainly have disadvantages compared to living hunter-gatherer or within an ancient empire, but the end state will be better. The Technocracy is the faction of universal progress. The Traditions are dangerous people set in outdated ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then by that argument what good did the Technocracy actually do? If recent modern technology is actually magic neutral and would have been discovered and developed by the non-magical types regardless instead of being mass produced magic that can be used by non-awakened beings the 'benevolent' Technocracy churned out for them it has officially never done a single good thing in its existence. Its crusade to wipe out the other traditions of magic so it can make the world a better place is officially just self-aggrandizing nonsense spewed while cynically removing potential political rivals instead of them seeking to tightly control the human consensus on reality to make sure their goodies they give out to the non-awakened don't potentially get interfered with down the line by a consensus shift. You have literally created the worst possible Technocracy where their good point is a lie they peddle to take credit for the achievements of the non-awakened creating tools that would have worked regardless of the state of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491196#post1491196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to conflate &quot;progressivism&quot; with &quot;being nice&quot;. And then you throw in a &quot;fascists&quot; as a way to justify it, to justapose progressivism with fascism and to try to make it look like those are polar opposites, when in fact they are not.<br /> <br /> Every single revolutionaire is a progressive, and every progressive is at least a bit revolutionaire. The idea is, after all, to &quot;push society foward&quot;, going away with the old and introducing the new.<br /> <br /> Now, a healthy society will have a healthy balance between keeping their traditions and changing and adapting. Societies too stifled with conservatism becomes suffocated and unable to change, and will be buried by an ever changing world. That's what happened to the chinese empire for example.<br /> <br /> Societies too hellbent on change however will simply consume themselves into a revolutionare frenzy. And oh boy, the &quot;progressives&quot; when such thing happens are much much worse than Mussolini - and even worse than Hitler sometimes. That's what happened with the French Revolution and their &quot;Terror&quot;, with hundreds of thousands beheaded in the name of &quot;progress&quot;. That's what happened in the USSR and China with dozens of MILLIONS of deaths.<br /> <br /> Progressives can and often are absolutely fascists. One thing does NOT exclude the other at all.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Techbocracy is beyond any doubt, both Progressive AND Fascist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what progress was made in the recent revolution where Iraq was taken over by religious fundamentalists and dragged kicking and screaming back into being a repressive theocracy? Mere social movement is not progress, movement can go in directions other then forward. The people running a 'revolution' can want to drag others kicking and screaming backwards on the progress meter by removing social rights actual progressives making progress had worked to obtain for people. So no, I disagree with your assertion that all social change is progressive when often that movement is going backwards towards a cliff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:12:54-07:00","id":1491209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491199#post1491199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hive mind technocracy would fail. In part, because there's not (yet?) The ability to maintain a network of agents in a way that cannot be disrupted. At least for now, the technocracy needs individual agents to be individuals with agency in order to be able to react to the unexpected. That said, the hive mind idea is something that upper management, at least, would be looking into. You see it in threat null, for example; where Transhumanity is a hive mind. But then, the concept behind threat null is that it is the technocracy taken closer to its logical extreme \u2014 and implementation of the 1e concept of the technocracy, where the agents are monsters that have been scrubbed of their humanity. The actual technocracy isn't that far gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I failed to properly explain &quot;Hivemind&quot; under quotes. The Hivemind would be Threat Null, the ultimate stage of transhumanism taken to its extreme.<br /> <br /> What I meant was more like a group of individuals absolutely brainwashed to all think alike - a real 1984 stuff, instead of being literally mind linked all the time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:22:51-07:00","id":1491213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491209#post1491209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I failed to properly explain &quot;Hivemind&quot; under quotes. The Hivemind would be Threat Null, the ultimate stage of transhumanism taken to its extreme.<br /> <br /> What I meant was more like a group of individuals absolutely brainwashed to all think alike - a real 1984 stuff, instead of being literally mind linked all the time</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the biggest weakness is that if everyone in your employ thinks <i>exactly </i>alike then your enemies are going to have an easy time targeting blind spots that exist in all your employees thought processes. &quot;Everyone knows those brainwashed technocrat drones are brainwashed to react to stimuli X in way Y so you can easily bait them into doing it then hit them with Z'. And sure, they can patch their drone software to plug up these holes but new ones will always be discovered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:58:54-07:00","id":1491220,"title":"","content":"While it's true that modern technology would have been developed anyway (and in the real world, it was), you do have to apply a little bit of suspension of disbelief. In this case, the idea is that in the world of darkness, modern technology would otherwise have taken longer to develop; and the technocracy is largely responsible for it having gotten developed as quickly as it did. Mage, or at least mages, tend to assume that Sleepers aren't able to do much on their own \u2014 that, as I mentioned in my last post, they're somewhat infantile, since they're not Awakened. In a particularly dark take on the World of Darkness, that may even be true to an extent. Certainly, Mage has a tendency to attribute a lot of real world developments to mages: the theory of relativity was the doing of the void engineers; quantum mechanics was invented by the Society of ether; LSD came from the children of knowledge (or perhaps the cult of ecstasy; that one's a little bit fuzzy). Heck, the entire imperialist March of the 19th century British Empire is laid at the feet of the late order of reason, early technocracy. Again, none of these are true in the real world. But Mage isn't the real world, however much it may look like it superficially. So allowances have to be made.<br /> <br /> In particular, it's bad form to choose to attribute all of the bad things that happened to a Mage faction without a tributing any of the good things that happened to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T11:40:27-07:00","id":1491224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491220#post1491220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's true that modern technology would have been developed anyway (and in the real world, it was), you do have to apply a little bit of suspension of disbelief. In this case, the idea is that in the world of darkness, modern technology would otherwise have taken longer to develop; and the technocracy is largely responsible for it having gotten developed as quickly as it did. Mage, or at least mages, tend to assume that Sleepers aren't able to do much on their own \u2014 that, as I mentioned in my last post, they're somewhat infantile, since they're not Awakened. In a particularly dark take on the World of Darkness, that may even be true to an extent. Certainly, Mage has a tendency to attribute a lot of real world developments to mages: the theory of relativity was the doing of the void engineers; quantum mechanics was invented by the Society of ether; LSD came from the children of knowledge (or perhaps the cult of ecstasy; that one's a little bit fuzzy). Heck, the entire imperialist March of the 19th century British Empire is laid at the feet of the late order of reason, early technocracy. Again, none of these are true in the real world. But Mage isn't the real world, however much it may look like it superficially. So allowances have to be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always a strange balance given how much various Mage factions are supposedly responsible for and how much the Technocracy is supposed to have driven the modern paradigm and its technology. If all modern technology would have developed anyways it neuters much the the effect of the Technocracy and the stakes of the Ascension War. If it is all due to the Technocracy, then sleepers are just a bunch of sheep to be led around by the nose.<br /> <br /> I think the best way of looking at it is that something would have developed anyways, and it would have performed many of the same functions as modern technology but it would have operated differently and on different principles. Networks of telegraph and telephone lines might not crisscross the world, but some kind of mass communication system would, whether based on electricity, imps, or the methodical torture of young kings (Pratchett Reference). Guns and bombs might not be used in every war, but some kind of long range armament would.<br /> <br /> In other words, the desire and interest largely comes from humanity while the particular ways of fulfilling those desires can be largely driven by Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T11:59:30-07:00","id":1491226,"title":"","content":"That's part of it; but the other part, as I see it, is that it would not have developed as quickly as it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T12:07:29-07:00","id":1491227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491226#post1491226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's part of it; but the other part, as I see it, is that it would not have developed as quickly as it did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. The Technocracy provided both intentionality and qualified safety from the monsters of the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T13:09:29-07:00","id":1491234,"title":"","content":"Technology breeds more technology. If a war devestated the top chip manufactueres in east asia, we'd be set back half a decade at least: the best microchips are made in two countries, the best microengineers are in these two countries, It's an industry that eats tens of billions of dollars. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy are going to hurl money into this stuff. They can also hurl Magick at it and make the process more efficient. The better the mundane technology, the less vulgar the hypertech, the less the technocracy need to rely on hypertech. A hypertech phone 20 years ago probably reaches the capabilities of what a phone does now, so imagine what a hypertech phone can do now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T14:09:39-07:00","id":1491239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491234#post1491234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technology breeds more technology. If a war devestated the top chip manufactueres in east asia, we'd be set back half a decade at least: the best microchips are made in two countries, the best microengineers are in these two countries, It's an industry that eats tens of billions of dollars.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy are going to hurl money into this stuff. They can also hurl Magick at it and make the process more efficient. The better the mundane technology, the less vulgar the hypertech, the less the technocracy need to rely on hypertech. <b>A hypertech phone 20 years ago probably reaches the capabilities of what a phone does now, so imagine what a hypertech phone can do now?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, people are apparently so bummed that we don't have flying cars yet its starting to impact what they believe is possible with the future of science and making it more difficult to do things with hyper tech in public. Its pretty hilarious actually, the Technocrats have done such a good job stamping out belief in the 'scientifically impossible' that it has started to come back to bite them in the ass when they claim they are just using 'advanced prototype technology' and lay people are like 'that is BS, we are nowhere near having the technology to make teleportation belts and guns that shoot freeze rays' so they get smacked with a vulgar magic penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:04:58-07:00","id":1491245,"title":"","content":"Flying cars are dumb as fuck and it baffles me that people thought we'd be using them by now. It should be noted that Dubai has hovercraft... and nobody else has adopted this technology because it's fucking stupid. Dubai just likes novelties because tourism. <br /> <br /> But then again 4k TVs are the norm and 8k TVs exist so we can't expect rationality when it comes to technology. Though I suppose from a seller's perspective it makes total sense to push this direction and from a consumer's point of view if you want a superior OLED and you can only buy OLEDs if they're big and 4k... Like it makes business sense even if t doesn't make common sense. <br /> <br /> <br /> On the flipside of things, it's very strange we haven't made killbots yet. All these drones and yet neither Robocop nor T-600s? What even is the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T19:22:53-07:00","id":1491266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491245#post1491245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flying cars are dumb as fuck and it baffles me that people thought we'd be using them by now. It should be noted that Dubai has hovercraft... and nobody else has adopted this technology because it's fucking stupid. Dubai just likes novelties because tourism.<br /> <br /> But then again 4k TVs are the norm and 8k TVs exist so we can't expect rationality when it comes to technology. Though I suppose from a seller's perspective it makes total sense to push this direction and from a consumer's point of view if you want a superior OLED and you can only buy OLEDs if they're big and 4k... Like it makes business sense even if t doesn't make common sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the flipside of things, it's very strange we haven't made killbots yet. All these drones and yet neither Robocop nor T-600s? What even is the point?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/fUImvprq-6M\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/fUImvprq-6M\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/fUImvprq-6M\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/fUImvprq-6M </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Those things look like a death trap to me, I can see why the technology isn't spreading.<br /> <br /> Because dropping bombs on people is easier then making a robot with human range motion in its extremities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T01:01:45-07:00","id":1491281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491224#post1491224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's always a strange balance given how much various Mage factions are supposedly responsible for and how much the Technocracy is supposed to have driven the modern paradigm and its technology. If all modern technology would have developed anyways it neuters much the the effect of the Technocracy and the stakes of the Ascension War. If it is all due to the Technocracy, then sleepers are just a bunch of sheep to be led around by the nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's not just the Technocracy that are this hubristic, but in fact it's EVERY single Mage.<br /> <br /> Mages are the elites, after all. The Sleepers are just that... The masses of ignorant peasants, who are just like ignorant children playing with matches.<br /> <br /> And I cant really blame Mages all too much for it. Just imagine how it would feel to have the keys for reality itself at the palm of your hand, knowing the deep mysteries of the Universe while you are surrounded by countless hordes of blinded imbeciles that needed to be guided into how to use rocks or clean their asses properly. I mean seriously, just think about that for a moment, let us imagine for a moment that we were one of the Awakened. And now, for each one of us, there's 1 million of blinded idiots.<br /> <br /> That's why I say that Mages are the worse kind of critters in the WoD - yes, worse than vampires. Because vampires are parasites, yes, it's a disease. But that's it for them, it's a societal sickness, but it's an alien infection.<br /> <br /> Mages however are <i>benevolent tyrants</i>. Every single one of them. And how would they not? If YOU knew the TRUTH - not one truth, not some truth but THE truth - how could you not become a tyrant?<br /> <br /> &quot;I know what's best for you... Better than yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> A &quot;benevolent&quot; tyrant is by far the worse type of despot. A rob Baron can have his hunger for power and luxury temporarily satiated, thus leaving his victims alone from time to time, but a &quot;benevolent&quot; tyrant will have his own consciousness as a guide to his atrocities. &quot;For the greater good&quot; is the root of the greatest evils. That's how the Soviet Union and China killed dozens of millions, they had &quot;The Plan&quot;, which was perfect and morally good, thus opposing &quot;The Plan&quot; was obviously morally evil. And, when you're doing things with a &quot;good&quot; purpose and fighting &quot;evil&quot;, oh boy, you can do no wrong.<br /> <br /> Everything becomes justifiable when it is for &quot;the greater good&quot;. So it's no wonder to me that the big evils in the WoD are NOT bloodsucking vampires or furious shapeshifters or alien Fae, but rather totalitarian Mages. Because Mages are the &quot;good guys&quot; ALWAYS, therefore opposing a Mage is opposing good itself; therefore, ANYTHING that doesnt fit EXACTLY in the worldviews of these guys is obviously evil, and has no room in this world.<br /> <br /> That's 100% the type of thinking of both fascism and socialism; if you oppose their great view of Utopia, you are an &quot;enemy of progress&quot; and must be squashed like a roach before your &quot;evil&quot; is allowed to contaminate others.<br /> <br /> And no, the Traditions or the Crafts are no different, and they would (and they did) do exactly like the Technocracy does; it's inevitable, it's in their nature to be and do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T02:24:52-07:00","id":1491284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491281#post1491281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, the Traditions or the Crafts are no different, and they would (and they did) do exactly like the Technocracy does; it's inevitable, it's in their nature to be and do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um. The whole point of Mage and the Council creed is to go above and beyond the petty and the human and to be BETTER. Sure there is zealotry and bigotry to overcome (I often argue that traditions still have more to do), but at the end of the day Mage is about being BETTER humans and making a BETTER world.<br /> <br /> So no, your view is quite wrong. Mage is about fixing yourself and fixing the world. You can go about and faff with awesome cosmic power and fuck other people up, but at the end of the day that's not what Ascension, personal or communal is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T04:18:13-07:00","id":1491286,"title":"","content":"The Path of Thorns, as described by Brucato, is precisely about <i>not</i> letting your hubris get the better of you. It's an extremely difficult path to walk precisely <i>because</i> it's so easy to fall into hubris, that you can end up doing so without realizing it. Good intentions aren't <i>nearly</i> enough; as Kakost said, some of the greatest atrocities in the world have been motivated by good intentions. <br /> <br /> And the Traditions, for all of their high-minded ideals, aren't immune to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T05:39:06-07:00","id":1491289,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> You are correct that any Mage can be a benevolent or not-so-benevolent tyrant and that many of them do. You are overstating it, though. There's nothing in the Mage condition that pushes them to be tyrants and it is not the only way that they can abuse their powers. <br /> <br /> What they do have, and what we as humans have, is the strong tendency to assume their opinions are correct. Those opinions do not always lend themselves to tyranny. Sometimes they lead to the opposite problem, that of callously ignoring the world. Indeed, one of the common complaints about the pre-Traditions was that they didn't concern themselves with the world or the people therein. <br /> <br /> Nor can we just say that changing the world (or for that matter retreating from it) is inherently tyrannical. The method also matters. Some mages try to convince the people to embrace the idea of a better world. Some try to coerce the people into accepting one they wouldn't otherwise accept. In typical Mage fashion, the Technocracy and Traditions complicate matters by doing both. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T06:38:58-07:00","id":1491292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491286#post1491286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Path of Thorns, as described by Brucato, is precisely about <i>not</i> letting your hubris get the better of you. It's an extremely difficult path to walk precisely <i>because</i> it's so easy to fall into hubris, that you can end up doing so without realizing it. Good intentions aren't <i>nearly</i> enough; as Kakost said, some of the greatest atrocities in the world have been motivated by good intentions.<br /> <br /> And the Traditions, for all of their high-minded ideals, aren't immune to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if that is a response to me, but i never said the Traditions were free of bullshit, just the other day we even discussed how I have a poorer view of how cosmopolitan and dedicated to the ideals of the Council the Traditions really are. My whole statement was in relation to the conclusion that Mages are the worst people and will forever be that - their evil is simple human evil and corruption by power and nearsightedness<br /> <br /> The whole Path of Thorns as a Road to Ascension is about the fact that to do it you need to be better than the average man, you need to go above your hubris, above your conciets and fixations. And most never do because they're satisfied with simple power forever blocking their way forward. However, the game is called The Ascension because this is the goal they are fighting for and they aspire to, and the goals of the Council (compared to the goals of the Traditions) are quite positive and inclusive and help on getting through some of the hurdles of the Path of Thorns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T07:48:44-07:00","id":1491301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491284#post1491284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um. The whole point of Mage and the Council creed is to go above and beyond the petty and the human and to be BETTER. Sure there is zealotry and bigotry to overcome (I often argue that traditions still have more to do), but at the end of the day Mage is about being BETTER humans and making a BETTER world.<br /> <br /> So no, your view is quite wrong. Mage is about fixing yourself and fixing the world. You can go about and faff with awesome cosmic power and fuck other people up, but at the end of the day that's not what Ascension, personal or communal is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You just confirmed everything I said. &quot;Making a better world&quot; = for the greater good. That's EXACTLY the hubristic thought process of the Technocracy too. The Union too wants to make a better world, you know?<br /> <br /> The communists of the Soviet Union, China, Korea, Cuba, they all sought to create a &quot;better world&quot;.<br /> <br /> You just confirmed my argument. Yes, the Traditions and the Crafts want to create a &quot;better world&quot;. But guess what? So do too does the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It is precisely because Mages seek to create a &quot;better world&quot; that they are tyrants! The only difference between the Traditions and Crafts to the Technocracy, is that they lack power, thus why they can be &quot;heroes&quot;. While they are revolutionaires they are &quot;heroes&quot;. If they were to ever win their &quot;revolution&quot;, they would become as much of despots as the Union. And the reason why I already said: because they are above the ignorant masses, they are the &quot;Enlightned&quot; after all, the &quot;Awaken&quot;. Mages know better, they know what's best for the ignorant peasants better than the &quot;peasants&quot; themselves.<br /> <br /> I mean, who are these people to have the presumptiom of even knowing what is BETTER? &quot;A better world&quot;. Look how presumptious that is - as if they were the moral judges of good and evil.<br /> <br /> And yes, this is also true in real life too. People constantly claiming to want to make a &quot;better world&quot; are all potential candidates of dictators. As if they were the moral judges of what's good and what's evil.<br /> <br /> So, what you said just reinforces my argument","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:03:36-07:00","id":1491303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491289#post1491289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> You are correct that any Mage can be a benevolent or not-so-benevolent tyrant and that many of them do. You are overstating it, though. There's nothing in the Mage condition that pushes them to be tyrants and it is not the only way that they can abuse their powers. <br /> <br /> What they do have, and what we as humans have, is the strong tendency to assume their opinions are correct. Those opinions do not always lend themselves to tyranny. Sometimes they lead to the opposite problem, that of callously ignoring the world. Indeed, one of the common complaints about the pre-Traditions was that they didn't concern themselves with the world or the people therein. <br /> <br /> Nor can we just say that changing the world (or for that matter retreating from it) is inherently tyrannical. The method also matters. Some mages try to convince the people to embrace the idea of a better world. Some try to coerce the people into accepting one they wouldn't otherwise accept. In typical Mage fashion, the Technocracy and Traditions complicate matters by doing both. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Mages typically care only about their worldview, which they consider immutable and unquestionable truths. Dreamspeakers for example are represented as the &quot;noble savages&quot;, yet they would let entire villages be slaughtered if only it were to bring harmony to the spirit world. The Chakravanti and Akashic went to war because they just simply could not tolerate one's another view of how society should be organized. The same goes for Choristers, Hermetics and Verbena.<br /> <br /> Notice also how the Ascension War is a GENOCIDAL WAR. It's a war of extermination - the goal is simple: the decimation of the opposition. It is not a limited war for territories or resources. It's a war for entirely ending the other side.<br /> <br /> Only ideological wars are extermination wars. Such are the cases of religious wars, or the infamous WW2. Most of the other wars in history were wars of conquest, not extermination.<br /> <br /> This means that Mages simply cannot tolerate opposing views. Yes, this is a human thing, not a &quot;Mage&quot; thing, because in the end, Mages are the most humans of the critters in the WoD. So yes, this is not inherent in Mages, but rather it is inherent in HUMANS, which is even more scary. And Mages are, indeed, humans. They are NOT some alien monsters touched by some extra dimensional curse. Mages are humans with unlocked potential. Which is why their shortcomings are all too human too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:04:47-07:00","id":1491304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491301#post1491301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just confirmed everything I said. &quot;Making a better world&quot; = for the greater good. That's EXACTLY the hubristic thought process of the Technocracy too. The Union too wants to make a better world, you know?<br /> <br /> The communists of the Soviet Union, China, Korea, Cuba, they all sought to create a &quot;better world&quot;.<br /> <br /> You just confirmed my argument. Yes, the Traditions and the Crafts want to create a &quot;better world&quot;. But guess what? So do too does the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It is precisely because Mages seek to create a &quot;better world&quot; that they are tyrants! The only difference between the Traditions and Crafts to the Technocracy, is that they lack power, thus why they can be &quot;heroes&quot;. While they are revolutionaires they are &quot;heroes&quot;. If they were to ever win their &quot;revolution&quot;, they would become as much of despots as the Union. And the reason why I already said: because they are above the ignorant masses, they are the &quot;Enlightned&quot; after all, the &quot;Awaken&quot;. Mages know better, they know what's best for the ignorant peasants better than the &quot;peasants&quot; themselves.<br /> <br /> I mean, who are these people to have the presumptiom of even knowing what is BETTER? &quot;A better world&quot;. Look how presumptious that is - as if they were the moral judges of good and evil.<br /> <br /> And yes, this is also true in real life too. People constantly claiming to want to make a &quot;better world&quot; are all potential candidates of dictators. As if they were the moral judges of what's good and what's evil.<br /> <br /> So, what you said just reinforces my argument</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You're decidedly missing the point. When I say BETTER I mean BETTER in a transhumanist way. Not in a petty my dad is better than your dad oneupmanship. Ascension is about going past prejudice, hubris and enforcing your way on others. All of those things are stumbling stones along the Way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:12:02-07:00","id":1491305,"title":"","content":"With all due respect, Kakost: no, it doesn't. Just because all mages have the <i>temptation</i> to meddle in mortal affairs unasked, that doesn't mean that all mages <i>do</i> so. Hubris is a pitfall that all mages are in <i>danger</i> of falling into; but some avoid it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:20:59-07:00","id":1491306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491304#post1491304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. You're decidedly missing the point. When I say BETTER I mean BETTER in a transhumanist way. Not in a petty my dad is better than your dad oneupmanship. Ascension is about going past prejudice, hubris and enforcing your way on others. All of those things are stumbling stones along the Way.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, \u201cbetter in a transhumanist way\u201d <i>is</i> the sort of thing Kakost is talking about<b></b>: it's the sort of thing that sounds good on paper, but in practice can go wrong in <i>so</i> many ways that attempts to achieve transhumanism, even if they <i>succeed</i>, can end up with horrifying results. It's also not something to be imposed on others: the Road to Ascension that you referred to earlier is a personal one, and <i>has to be</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:26:14-07:00","id":1491307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491207#post1491207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what progress was made in the recent revolution where Iraq was taken over by religious fundamentalists and dragged kicking and screaming back into being a repressive theocracy? Mere social movement is not progress, movement can go in directions other then forward. The people running a 'revolution' can want to drag others kicking and screaming backwards on the progress meter by removing social rights actual progressives making progress had worked to obtain for people. So no, I disagree with your assertion that all social change is progressive when often that movement is going backwards towards a cliff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is the judge of what &quot;progress&quot; is? You?<br /> <br /> You see, this is my problem about progressism. It's this &quot;hollier-than-thou&quot; view of the world, the idea of being the judge of good and evil and to just simply know better. &quot;There is a line of progress, and we know how to get there!&quot;<br /> <br /> So, let us talk Iraq; other than the cynical reasons for the war - namely, oil - there were also the <b>progressive</b> justification about it too. Saddam Hussein was an awful dictator, he were a true maniac murderous psycopath. If you ever get the change of meeting an iraquian, ask them and they'll tell.<br /> <br /> So, the entire idea revolved around a sort of &quot;democratic crusade&quot;. That we, the beautiful people living in the clean democracies, should FORCE those poor people living in those horrible tyrannies to adopt our &quot;superior&quot; ways - wether they want to or not.<br /> <br /> &quot;They must learn and adopt our peaceful ways...<br /> ...BY FORCE!&quot;<br /> <br /> See what Im meaning?<br /> <br /> Yes, both Afghanistan and Iraq are the result of Progressivism at it's fullest. &quot;I know what's best for you... Better than you. So, you'll accept my help... Even if I have to force you&quot;.<br /> <br /> This reasoning is no different from socialism either; it's imposing a particular view of &quot;progress&quot; - and the opinions of the &quot;ignorant masses&quot;, as the progressivists view them, be damned.<br /> <br /> Just like Mages view the &quot;Sleepers&quot;. The &quot;Masses&quot;. Just notice how condescending this is. Mages are &quot;Awaken&quot; and &quot;Enlightned&quot;, while non mages are &quot;Sleepers&quot;. There is, they view themselves (not without some reason in this case thou) as above the pathetic common man - which aint too different from what &quot;intellectuals&quot; from real life view themselves by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:32:28-07:00","id":1491308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491306#post1491306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, \u201cbetter in a transhumanist way\u201d <i>is</i> the sort of thing Kakost is talking about<b></b>: it's the sort of thing that sounds good on paper, but in practice can go wrong in <i>so</i> many ways that attempts to achieve transhumanism, even if they <i>succeed</i>, can end up with horrifying results. It's also not something to be imposed on others: the Road to Ascension that you referred to earlier is a personal one, and <i>has to be</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I can agree there. Transhumanism is a loaded word, especially as in general fiction it's closely tied to scientific ideals and post human development. I mean it in a more general sense of going beyond the traditional failings of humanity and becoming better on a spiritual and cosmic scale. As such Ascension is likely a deeply intimate experience, and one that's not applicable from one human to another. Any form of &quot;Joint Ascension&quot; of humanity is something that can only work if you help others along the way and allow them to make their own choices and revelations. In so far I like the ideals of the Council because they believe everyone should have this freedom of choice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:35:28-07:00","id":1491309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491304#post1491304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. You're decidedly missing the point. When I say BETTER I mean BETTER in a transhumanist way. Not in a petty my dad is better than your dad oneupmanship. Ascension is about going past prejudice, hubris and enforcing your way on others. All of those things are stumbling stones along the Way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am aware of that. I guess the quote &quot;you either die a hero or you live long enough to see yourself become the villain&quot; holds too much truth here. The Order of Reason once were the noble heroes &quot;fighting the good fight&quot;. When THEY were the ones who were the revolutionaires. As soon as they grabbed reality by it's balls, they turned reality into its bitch.<br /> <br /> The Traditions can be the heroes of their own story and &quot;fight the good fight&quot; - <i>as long as they &quot;rage against the machine&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> If they were to ever become the System, they would fail to achieve their noble goals thou.<br /> <br /> Because power attracts the worse, and corrupts the better ones.<br /> <br /> Again, that's not a Mage thing, but rather a Human thing (which is what Mages essentially are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T08:50:02-07:00","id":1491311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491303#post1491303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Mages typically care only about their worldview, which they consider immutable and unquestionable truths.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Traditions, in particular, foster the notion that any particular Tradition's worldview is <i>not</i> an immutable and unquestionable truth. Their ability to cooperate with each other <i>depends</i> on the individuals each being able to say \u201c\u2026but I might be wrong\u201d. That's an implication of \u201cwe're all doing the same thing, just in different ways\u201d; and a smart Traditionist will keep that in mind. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491303#post1491303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreamspeakers for example are represented as the &quot;noble savages&quot;, yet they would let entire villages be slaughtered if only it were to bring harmony to the spirit world. The Chakravanti and Akashic went to war because they just simply could not tolerate one's another view of how society should be organized. The same goes for Choristers, Hermetics and Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div> Note that the Himalayan Wars <i>ended a long time ago.</i> By the time of the Sorcerers Crusade, they were able to get along well enough to join the Traditions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491303#post1491303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice also how the Ascension War is a GENOCIDAL WAR. It's a war of extermination - the goal is simple: the decimation of the opposition. It is not a limited war for territories or resources. It's a war for entirely ending the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that simple; but to the extent that it's true, it's one-sided. At the height of the Pogrom, if the Traditions had stopped fighting, they would have been wiped out; if the Technocracy had stopped fighting\u2026 well, we don't have to speculate on that one: they <i>did</i> stop fighting, in 1999 when the Reckoning came. During the \u201chot stage\u201d of the Ascension War, the Technocracy was the aggressor and the Traditions were merely trying to survive. The two are not morally equivalent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491303#post1491303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only ideological wars are extermination wars. Such are the cases of religious wars, or the infamous WW2. Most of the other wars in history were wars of conquest, not extermination.<br /> <br /> This means that Mages simply cannot tolerate opposing views.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb; as a tendency. <i>Not</i> as an absolute, unbreakable fact. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491303#post1491303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is a human thing, not a &quot;Mage&quot; thing, because in the end, Mages are the most humans of the critters in the WoD. So yes, this is not inherent in Mages, but rather it is inherent in HUMANS, which is even more scary. And Mages are, indeed, humans. They are NOT some alien monsters touched by some extra dimensional curse. Mages are humans with unlocked potential. Which is why their shortcomings are all too human too</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, this is why I don't have as much of a problem with \u201cthus and such in the real world is <i>actually</i> a mage's doing in the World of Darkness\u201d as I do with \u201cthus and such in the real world is <i>actually</i> a vampire's doing in the World of Darkness\u201d. Of all of the World of Darkness gamelines, with the possible exception of Hunter, Mage is perhaps the most purely representative of human nature. And \u201cmages did it\u201d merely personifies the real-world factors at play, instead of undermining them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-25-2022, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T10:39:47-07:00","id":1491316,"title":"","content":"Kakost... you're talking a lot of wrong. Did the conquistadors conquer south America to save it from savagery or did they do it for the literal mountain of silver. They did it for the literal mountain of silver and all claims of doing it to civilize child sacrificing heathens, true or not, are a convenient excuse to tell the people back home they're not massacring natives just for an obscene amount of wealth. Liberal causes will always be used to justify amoral and reactionary evil. Your local bigots don't become liberals because they want to &quot;save the children&quot; and &quot;protect the family&quot;. And for all the attention-drawing populism and racism the Nazis pulled their regime was ultimately propped up to create and consolidate the fortunes of leaders, close friends and party members by placing key industries under their care at the expense of the rest of the country. Hitler doesn't become a good guy in a world where everyone's a blue eyed German following the same traditions, he'd still be a piece of shit. There are very few examples in history where genuine ideologues ruin everything for their people: the overwhelming majority of the time it's just selfish people using a few appealing ideas to mask what they really want to do. <br /> <br /> <br /> Ergo, a genuinely benevolent dictator is obviously better than a robber baron. I can't fully express within the confines of the forum rules how utterly absurd it is to think the other way round. Any reservations towards a genuinely benevolent dictator are either written with guilt or are more concerned with how genuine the benevolence is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T10:49:30-07:00","id":1491318,"title":"","content":"So there's no validity to the saying that the road to Hell is paved with good intentions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:09:01-07:00","id":1491323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who is the judge of what &quot;progress&quot; is? You?<br /> <br /> You see, this is my problem about progressism. It's this &quot;hollier-than-thou&quot; view of the world, the idea of being the judge of good and evil and to just simply know better. &quot;There is a line of progress, and we know how to get there!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile you wouldn't dream of judging another person's views and telling them they are wrong, right? Literally everything you have been posting is nothing but pure hypocrisy. You lambast me for being self-righteous and having the gall to dare judge myself fit to judge right and wrong then go on paragraphs long self-righteous screeds casting judgement on me on the basis that you know right from wrong better then me and that I have it wrong. As is always the case when people try to use moral relativism to cover for people with nasty views while hoping nobody is smart enough to point out that if you really believed that kind of thing you'd never criticize <b>anybody </b>because you believe everyone is equally right because morality is relative. Instead you selectively rail against the progressive while ignoring anyone else that wants to impose their version of morality on others, almost as if you are running a scam where you pretend to be a moral relativist because you think it will make your argument land better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, let us talk Iraq; other than the cynical reasons for the war - namely, oil - there were also the <b>progressive</b> justification about it too. Saddam Hussein was an awful dictator, he were a true maniac murderous psycopath. If you ever get the change of meeting an iraquian, ask them and they'll tell.<br /> <br /> So, the entire idea revolved around a sort of &quot;democratic crusade&quot;. That we, the beautiful people living in the clean democracies, should FORCE those poor people living in those horrible tyrannies to adopt our &quot;superior&quot; ways - wether they want to or not.<br /> <br /> &quot;They must learn and adopt our peaceful ways...<br /> ...BY FORCE!&quot; </div> </div> </div>You do realize that not a single damn person ever actually believed that particular justification Dubya spun out to pretty up his fiasco, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-25-2022, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:27:32-07:00","id":1491327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491318#post1491318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's no validity to the saying that the road to Hell is paved with good intentions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there is, but no sense in being reductive here. There is a whole spectrum of ethics and morality at play in Mage and the characters within can fulfill many roles within that spectrum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:30:21-07:00","id":1491328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491316#post1491316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kakost... you're talking a lot of wrong. Did the conquistadors conquer south America to save it from savagery or did they do it for the literal mountain of silver. They did it for the literal mountain of silver and all claims of doing it to civilize child sacrificing heathens, true or not, are a convenient excuse to tell the people back home they're not massacring natives just for an obscene amount of wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. You see, the Roman Empire, as Nietzsche well put, had a what he called &quot;Masters Morality&quot;. Just like the Huns, Aztecs, Monghols, Chinese, Japanese Empire, Nazis. Those were unapologetic towards their savagery. They attacked neighbors and conquered and enslaved with the only moral imperative that they can. They were strong, neighbors were weak, and that's all that mattered.<br /> <br /> Christian civilization and islamic civilization however are &quot;Slave Morality&quot; civilizations. While Master civilizations pride strenght and personal achievement, Slave civilizations pride piety.<br /> <br /> So, all of a sudden &quot;I want slaves for the glory of Rome&quot; was no longer enough of a justification for conquest.<br /> <br /> Yes, the spaniards Conquistadors were little more than criminal pirates, mercenaries and cutthroat thugs of the worse kind seeking to fill their pockets with gold, but they werent the only ones to settle the New World. There were also priests seeking to convert and educate the natives. Now, we may judge that with hindsight and using our modern day moralities all we want, but those are nevertheless NOT the actions of people that seek to subjulgate others for the sole purpose of seeking power and wealth<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491316#post1491316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liberal causes will always be used to justify amoral and reactionary evil. Your local bigots don't become liberals because they want to &quot;save the children&quot; and &quot;protect the family&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very Marxist idea, the Materialism of Karl Marx, the idea that basically everything about society revolves around economic factors.<br /> <br /> Sadly, this idea, along pretty much everything that Marx wrote, is WRONG.<br /> <br /> It completely disregards cultural factors alltogheter, which is rather absurd.<br /> <br /> Throughout history, shame, glory and vengeance were powerful motivators for conflicts. It's not just simply because &quot;lets see if there's a pile of gold over there&quot;. Explorers during the Great Navigations truly believed they were doing &quot;God's work&quot; by exploring the unknow, and that was NOT just a cynical justification for their actions, they truly believed in it. The islamic conquests werent just countless genocides in order to open up &quot;free estate&quot; and gather slaves while using Islam as a cynical excuse. They TRULY believed that their expansionist Jihad was the will of Allah.<br /> <br /> Dont be so fast to judge other people's motives based on your wordview, because that will distort the facts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491316#post1491316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for all the attention-drawing populism and racism the Nazis pulled their regime was ultimately propped up to create and consolidate the fortunes of leaders, close friends and party members by placing key industries under their care at the expense of the rest of the country. Hitler doesn't become a good guy in a world where everyone's a blue eyed German following the same traditions, he'd still be a piece of shit. There are very few examples in history where genuine ideologues ruin everything for their people: the overwhelming majority of the time it's just selfish people using a few appealing ideas to mask what they really want to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, that's absolutely false. First of all, the nazis werent just a bunch of gangsters that decided to use some bogus mambo jambo to deceive the masses in a mere power grab move. To believe that is to downplay what nazism represents.<br /> <br /> No, the Nazis were TRUE believers in their own bullshit. Nazism was actually a cult based on a 19th century pseudoscientific bullshit idea called &quot;Teosophy&quot; (Google it, Im not making this up, you'll be impressed with the amount of lunacy in that crap. The SS leader Himmler for example, were a fanatical zealot of Teosophy and acted nothing short of a cult leader. Yeah, the guy was even more a lunatic than people think.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the communists of Russia and China were also true believers. They werent just communists from &quot;out of the mouth&quot; (a brazilian saying, &quot;out of the amount&quot;, in appearance only). Lenin, and even Stalin and Mao, truly believed in the &quot;communist Utopia&quot;. Which is also why they believed that all of their crimes would eventually be forgiven once they achieved their paradise on Earth.<br /> <br /> Going a little further in time, the most ruthless monarchs of Spain for example were Isabela de Castille and Fernando de Aragon. The most pious of the spanish kings, the most ardent adepts of catholicism. The ones that turned the Spanish Inquisition into overdrive due to their zealotry.<br /> <br /> In Revolutionary France, the one that was know as &quot;The Incorruptible&quot;, the Jacobine leader Robespierre, who before getting power were vehemently against the death penalty and was one of the great advocates of the &quot;Enlightnement&quot;, became the dictator that introduced the government model under the subtle name of &quot;Terror&quot; and beheaded hundreds of thousands in public exhibitions of state brutality.<br /> <br /> Oh, there's one example I particularly like: Papa Doc, the dictator from Haiti. He was a humanist doctor before seizing power; after becoming dictator, he would spread the propaganda over the entire country that he was a LITERAL Scion of the Baron Samedi - AKA his State Propaganda was that he were the literal son of the Voodoum representation of DEATH.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491316#post1491316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ergo, a genuinely benevolent dictator is obviously better than a robber baron. I can't fully express within the confines of the forum rules how utterly absurd it is to think the other way round. Any reservations towards a genuinely benevolent dictator are either written with guilt or are more concerned with how genuine the benevolence is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? And where does such an angel of benevolence hides? Or could it be you? Or perhaps me?<br /> <br /> This to me is a gullible view of how power works. If you can, search &quot;Rules for Rulers&quot; on YouTube. It's a very short video - 15 min only - but that explains almost everything about how power works. And with it, you'll understand why there are no &quot;benevolent dictators&quot;, and also why the structures of power always prop up the worse Hitlers and Stalins around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:34:01-07:00","id":1491330,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy, this is getting heated\u2026<br /> <br /> Point of order: I'm pretty sure Kakost is the last person here who would advocate for moral relativism. Rather, what he seems to be talking about is moral <i>humility</i>; the opposite of hubris, and the opposite of dictating to others they should do. There's a bit of irony, as opposed to hypocrisy, in that, in a manner similar to how there's irony in tolerant people being intolerant of intolerant people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:38:01-07:00","id":1491331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491327#post1491327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course there is, but no sense in being reductive here. There is a whole spectrum of ethics and morality at play in Mage and the characters within can fulfill many roles within that spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually my point. Mizu appears to be getting rather reductionist about it; the post I responded to came across as saying that people with pure motives can do no wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:53:23-07:00","id":1491332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491323#post1491323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile you wouldn't dream of judging another person's views and telling them they are wrong, right? Literally everything you have been posting is nothing but pure hypocrisy. You lambast me for being self-righteous and having the gall to dare judge myself fit to judge right and wrong then go on paragraphs long self-righteous screeds casting judgement on me on the basis that you know right from wrong better then me and that I have it wrong. As is always the case when people try to use moral relativism to cover for people with nasty views while hoping nobody is smart enough to point out that if you really believed that kind of thing you'd never criticize <b>anybody </b>because you believe everyone is equally right because morality is relative. Instead you selectively rail against the progressive while ignoring anyone else that wants to impose their version of morality on others, almost as if you are running a scam where you pretend to be a moral relativist because you think it will make your argument land better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not judging you. If I gave that impression, I apologize. It was not my intention. What I was trying to convey is that NOBODY should try to impose their own views on others, no matter how self righteous a person may be - in fact, particularly self righteous people.<br /> <br /> I am sure that you and most people here in this forum are good people who would genuinely want to create a better world. And that's exactly where the danger lies. A good person after all, can do no wrong. That's the theme of the Technocracy after all. They are humanity's <b>last line of defense</b> after all. How far wouldnt YOU go, if you were the only thing standing on the way of chaos and destruction?<br /> <br /> When there are &quot;barbarians at the gates&quot;, there are no acts that cannot be justified for the sake of a bigger &quot;greater good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Im an Anarcho-capitalist brother. I believe myself to be right, I believe myself to have my mind and my heart in the right place, and I believe myself to be a good, ethical person. Just like the vast majority of non psychopathic human beings.<br /> <br /> And yet, I wouldnt trust myself with absolute power. Would you? Would you trust your entire life to be at the hands of another, even if this other is supposedly &quot;good&quot;? Would you trust me to have power your life and death?<br /> <br /> Well, I wouldnt trust you to have such power over me, and neither should you trust on me for that too.<br /> <br /> If I were to become the &quot;World's Emperor&quot;, would I be a &quot;benevolent despot&quot;?<br /> <br /> No. The answer is absolutely no. I am a good guy with a huge heart, and yet I do not trust I wouldnt become a monstruous maniac. And neither would you, nor the next guy.<br /> <br /> Cursed be the man that trusts in the son of the man.<br /> <br /> In the West we created systems to keep power in check against excesses, with systems of weights and counter weights, exactly because no single person can be trusted with power, and good intentions be damned.<br /> <br /> This is why I say that the moral absolutism of progressism, of having this idea of knowing what the ultimate good and evil are, is dangerous.<br /> <br /> And yes, I do pass judgment about what I believe good and evil to be, however I think that everybody must have the freedom to make their own choices without cohercion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:43:05-07:00","id":1491340,"title":"","content":"Mage is ultimately a game of Titans in the body of mortals. And every single one of their strugles, is an existential fight. For the Technocracy, it the Union falls, the Things-Men-Was-Not-Meant-To-Know will devour everything. For the Traditions, if the Technocracy wins, humanity will be utterly enslaved and all the flame of the potential within each person will be snuffled forever. Adding to this, each one of this individuals are idealists who are convinced they are right. There's just too much at stake for half measures here, it's an all or nothing proposition where the winner takes all, and the barbarians are constantly at the gates.<br /> <br /> In this it truly is important the notion of humility - particularly for those who are essentially Gods in human guise. And for that same reason, it's hard not to be caught up in their own greatness - but it is essential to do so. Truly heroic Mages must strive NOT to advocate for their own worldviews, but to respect the choices that others, even the &quot;Sleepers&quot; which they deem as lessers, do, even when such choice means that said Mages will be at the losing side of this game.<br /> <br /> This is a hard balance to achieve thou, trying to accept that the Sleepers have ultimately chosen the Technocratic Paradigm and rejected the alternatives presented by the Traditions or Crafts, and still deciding to &quot;fight the good fight&quot; against the Union nevertheless, but not to oppose the decision of the masses, but rather to make sure that the Union will also respect the &quot;people's decision&quot; too. And that's something that the Traditions (and the Crafts even more so) still need to learn and adapt to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T14:06:49-07:00","id":1491344,"title":"","content":"I would just point out, though, that the sleepers have not accepted the technocratic paradigm. If you look at World population, the vast majority of it is in Asia and Africa; North America is a relatively small percentage. To think that the essentially Western technocracy defines the consensus is its own little bit of hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:21:31-07:00","id":1491352,"title":"","content":"G<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491332#post1491332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im an Anarcho-capitalist brother.</div> </div> </div> </div>GLORY TO SET<br /> Oh, you mean in real life? You mean you belong to that one area of the political compass that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HTN64g9lA2g\" target=\"_blank\">could never actually work because the very concept is designed to swallow itself?</a> I dunno man i think it's really weird that you'd trust people to amass power and do the right thing for society without regulations while simultaneously not trusting well regulated smart people with a modicum of mandate to not screw you over for less than reasonable things. A well intentioned mage that wants to push society towards an ideal is significantly less scary than a mage that just wants power and will readily squash the little guy to get it, unless you're a criminal. &quot;The Greater good&quot; has it's problems but significantly less than &quot;leave me alone I'll do what I want&quot;. Mages will be worse for the rest of the world the more freedom granted to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:23:49-07:00","id":1491353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491344#post1491344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just point out, though, that the sleepers have not accepted the technocratic paradigm. If you look at World population, the vast majority of it is in Asia and Africa; North America is a relatively small percentage. To think that the essentially Western technocracy defines the consensus is its own little bit of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonably sure they are an international organization whose reach extends across the entire world, if they weren't a threat to places outside of Europe and North America why would organizations like the Akashic Brotherhood have bothered joining up with the other Traditions to defend their way of life against them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:40:11-07:00","id":1491356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491353#post1491353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reasonably sure they are an international organization whose reach extends across the entire world, if they weren't a threat to places outside of Europe and North America why would organizations like the Akashic Brotherhood have bothered joining up with the other Traditions to defend their way of life against them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a worldwide organization. But their worldview reflects that of North america. Not china, not india. And those two Nations alone have nearly 10 times the population of the United states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:55:04-07:00","id":1491358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491356#post1491356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are a worldwide organization. But their worldview reflects that of North america. Not china, not india. And those two Nations alone have nearly 10 times the population of the United states.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I worded that poorly. What I meant is that they are international in <i>membership</i>. They aren't just a bunch of Europeans and Americans trying to control the rest of the world remotely, they actually have global membership that agrees with the tenets of the Technocracy and is setting up a global New World Order in the shadows. Its like if all the conspiracy theories about the United Nations wanting to take over the world for a globalist NWO were true and being lead by people that could do magical super science and had a hate boner for people that just did regular magic.<br /> <br /> Edit: Best example of this, go look at page 88 of Technocracy Reloaded. Where it has an Asian operative in character from the setting going on about how there is no East West divide and confirming that the Technocracy has more Asians in it then Westerners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-25-2022, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:04:43-07:00","id":1491360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491352#post1491352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">G<br /> GLORY TO SET<br /> Oh, you mean in real life? You mean you belong to that one area of the political compass that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HTN64g9lA2g\" target=\"_blank\">could never actually work because the very concept is designed to swallow itself?</a> I dunno man i think it's really weird that you'd trust people to amass power and do the right thing for society without regulations while simultaneously not trusting well regulated smart people with a modicum of mandate to not screw you over for less than reasonable things. A well intentioned mage that wants to push society towards an ideal is significantly less scary than a mage that just wants power and will readily squash the little guy to get it, unless you're a criminal. &quot;The Greater good&quot; has it's problems but significantly less than &quot;leave me alone I'll do what I want&quot;. Mages will be worse for the rest of the world the more freedom granted to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>No Attacking Other Posters.</b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:18:44-07:00","id":1491366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491352#post1491352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">G<br /> GLORY TO SET<br /> Oh, you mean in real life? You mean you belong to that one area of the political compass that <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HTN64g9lA2g&amp;quot;]could</a> never actually work because the very concept is designed to swallow itself?[/URL] I dunno man i think it's really weird that you'd trust people to amass power and do the right thing for society without regulations while simultaneously not trusting well regulated smart people with a modicum of mandate to not screw you over for less than reasonable things. A well intentioned mage that wants to push society towards an ideal is significantly less scary than a mage that just wants power and will readily squash the little guy to get it, unless you're a criminal. &amp;quot;The Greater good&amp;quot; has it's problems but significantly less than &amp;quot;leave me alone I'll do what I want&amp;quot;. Mages will be worse for the rest of the world the more freedom granted to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. Yeah, Im an ancap in real life, precisely because I dont trust my Overlords enough to boss me around. The intrincacies of my political views I'll leave outside of the scope of this forum.<br /> <br /> I dont consent to being robbed by the criminal syndicate vulgarly know as &quot;government&quot;, and yet they do it no matter what despite my will, and I have to pay - or else.<br /> <br /> What I find it to be funny is that people dont trust politicians and believe them all to be corrupt, yet everybody expects the government, who is not a living entity but rather a collection of those same individuals who everybody believes to be untrustworthy, selfish and corrupt, everybody expects those same people to fix all of their problems.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Technocracy is the artistic representation of exactly the Government. They represent the CIA, the KGB, the Stasi and the SS, the &quot;Shadow Government&quot;; the idea of the MiB is a representation of the &quot;Fear of the State&quot;, the fear that the powers to be will kidnap you under the cover of the night for some unkown reason, put a black bag in your face, and you'll never be seem again.<br /> <br /> That's in fact an all too familiar fear for people who lived in former dictatorships (like Eastern Europe) or current ones (like Russia, China, Saudi Arabia etc etc).<br /> <br /> To be real, even in &quot;democracies&quot; people still fear the State. I mean, even in the USA or Europe, you can be as cocky as you want about being &quot;free&quot;, but anyone with at least an ounce of common sense will know better than to not be intimidated when is stopped by a police officer.<br /> <br /> Once again, the Technocracy was inspired by the 1984 book, which is a parody of the power of the State amplified to its maximum (personified by the USSR).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:29:21-07:00","id":1491367,"title":"","content":"The technocracy is several things. One of those things is a stand-in for the idea of a global government. Another thing is a stand in for economic elitism. Yet another is a stand-in for the transhumanist philosophy. That's part of what I was trying to get at with my earlier post about how each convention would approach the notion of transgenderism. The NWO would do what governments do, and would try to regulate the behavior of the people to resolve the difficulty; the progenitors would do what transhumanist biologists would do, and would try to adjust the biology to match the individuals desires; iteration X would do what the more mechanistic transhumanists would do, and try to upload the person's mind into a machine to perfect them. And the syndicates would see it as a revenue generator. Only the NWO would approach it from the perspective of a governing body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:08:31-07:00","id":1491373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491344#post1491344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just point out, though, that the sleepers have not accepted the technocratic paradigm. If you look at World population, the vast majority of it is in Asia and Africa; North America is a relatively small percentage. To think that the essentially Western technocracy defines the consensus is its own little bit of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had this discussion a few years ago in this same forum I believe (well, MANY years ago actually). And Im not saying that every single human in the planet is a student of evolutionary biology or astrophysics, but rather that, besides small numbers of truly isolated people living under tribes, pretty much everybody agrees that a smartphone can &quot;magically&quot; send written texts to the other side of the world almost instantaneously, and dont think too much about it.<br /> <br /> My argument however is that the setting of MtA is just simply outright WRONG. The problem is that the setting is modeled in the real world; the problem with this is that in the real world, scientific knowledge is a FACT rather than a weird conspiracy of miraculous men and women to create a smoke screen to hide the truth. My smartphone works because electrons ARE indeed being exchanged inside the circuits, and the Wi Fi actually DO send radio waves to satelites in space.<br /> <br /> In the setting of MtA, that's not true - smartphones work because everybody collectively believe that if you plug them into the grid, the &quot;magic happens&quot;, and they have correspondence links between one another. All the talk about &quot;radio waves&quot; is just technobabble.<br /> <br /> This creates a problem, because in the real world, technological advancement comes by scientific advancement, and that happens regardless of what people may believe. Relativity, Quantum Physics, all that would sound as superscience or even pseudoscience for a 19th century classical scientist, yet those were proven, regardless of personal belief. And today our GPS relies on relativity.<br /> <br /> That would not be the case for the world of MtA, where belief is what determine possibility, rather than possibility shaping belief.<br /> <br /> The problem is, this idea that scientificism - a blind faith on science that the Techies would want people to have - just simply aint a majority anywhere. Not even in the US or Europe. Not in the real world at least.<br /> <br /> Im a good example of it. I am an atheist. My wife is Umbandist, which is a brazilian religion with african origin - very similar to the caribbean Vodoo or Santeria, which probably are more known for you guys in the Northern Hemisphere. She believes in ancestral guiding spirits. In the West, Christianism is most prevalent, and as any religion, it has beliefs that are a matter of faith and go beyond the scope of scientific scrutiny, as well as belief in the supernatural and in miracles. Even discounting the christian majority, there are other minor religions, all with some sense of belief into the supernatural, and loose movements, like Wicca or New Age and other kinds of esoterism.<br /> <br /> Even people that declare themselves to be non religious or agnostic, there are still a huge plethora of non scientific beliefs, like astrology, numerology, homeopathy and some such that people adhere to.<br /> <br /> The fact is that only a tiny minority truly adhere to atheistic skeptic materialism, which is what it could be called the Technocratic Paradigm. The truth is that the setting of MtA gets it's core assumptions wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:24:30-07:00","id":1491376,"title":"","content":"I mean, I can't speak for anyone else, but I've never had much problem combining belief in God with belief in science. God gave us dominion and mastery over this world and, in my view, science is how we express that dominion. It is us bending the world God gave us to our will and being masters of it. Scientific discoveries are perfectly in line with God and not us turning away from Him like a bunch of people assert when they say things like 'you taking medicine instead of praying for God to take away the illness shows a lack of faith in God!'. Things like medicine and electronics are gifts God left us in this world to discover by learning of it and mastering it. And I am pretty sure that if I were a sleeper in MtA that would leave me as being perfectly in line with what Technocrats want in regards to making their technology function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-25-2022, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:24:46-07:00","id":1491377,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject of \u201cthings that I've addressed before\u201d, let me point you to my musings on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\"> the nature of the Consensus</a> (recently updated with links to another recent discussion where I elaborate on some of the dinner points). In a nutshell, there's reason to believe that the World of Darkness isn't quite as Consensus-driven as many believe it to be; and that the Enlightened Science of the Technocracy developed the way it did not <i>just</i> because the Technocracy pushed it, but also because the fabric of the Tapestry (as distinct from the Consensus) was predisposed to develop in that way <i>anyway</i>. <br /> <br /> In <i>that</i> view, the setting makes sense; <i>and</i> Enlightened Scientists (a larger group than just Technocrats) can be said to have a point when they claim that there's an objective foundation to reality, without invalidating the Traditions' position that it's all about Willworking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:34:56-07:00","id":1491380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491377#post1491377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the subject of \u201cthings that I've addressed before\u201d, let me point you to my musings on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\"> the nature of the Consensus</a> (recently updated with links to another recent discussion where I elaborate on some of the dinner points). In a nutshell, there's reason to believe that the World of Darkness isn't quite as Consensus-driven as many believe it to be; and that the Enlightened Science of the Technocracy developed the way it did not <i>just</i> because the Technocracy pushed it, but also because the fabric of the Tapestry (as distinct from the Consensus) was predisposed to develop in that way <i>anyway</i>.<br /> <br /> In <i>that</i> view, the setting makes sense; <i>and</i> Enlightened Scientists (a larger group than just Technocrats) can be said to have a point when they claim that there's an objective foundation to reality, without invalidating the Traditions' position that it's all about Willworking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats true, but they have made it pretty hard to figure out which bits of technology are based on the foundation and which bits are only possible because of the consensus so its kind of an annoying topic to ponder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-25-2022, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T18:09:17-07:00","id":1491383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491376#post1491376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I can't speak for anyone else, but I've never had much problem combining belief in God with belief in science. God gave us dominion and mastery over this world and, in my view, science is how we express that dominion. It is us bending the world God gave us to our will and being masters of it. Scientific discoveries are perfectly in line with God and not us turning away from Him like a bunch of people assert when they say things like 'you taking medicine instead of praying for God to take away the illness shows a lack of faith in God!'. Things like medicine and electronics are gifts God left us in this world to discover by learning of it and mastering it. And I am pretty sure that if I were a sleeper in MtA that would leave me as being perfectly in line with what Technocrats want in regards to making their technology function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the advent of the scientific method - aka &quot;science&quot; - came to be in Europe and not in the Middle East or the Kingdom of Congo or the Aztec Empire or in China because of the particularities of christianism. For Islam for instance, everything is just simply the &quot;will of Allah&quot;, therefore it doesnt make sense to try to &quot;decypher&quot; the universe if things are just simply whatever Allah wills it to be at any given moment.<br /> <br /> For Christianism however, the idea is that God created an understandable and RATIONAL world, which can be understood therefore using our reason.<br /> <br /> The birth of science therefore, arose as an attempt to better understand &quot;God's mind&quot; - a fact that my fellow atheists sadly disregard (and even worse, ridicule on many occasions).<br /> <br /> I wont be able to remember where I read it - Guide to the Technocracy, I dont know. But it did indeed have entries for agents who were believers of some faith - mostly christianism or islam, but also buddism, hinduism and others, and it said that, althought the Technocratic official policy was that of quiet tolerance (aka it's fine as long as you dont proselitize), the entry also stated that those were often ridiculed by their colleages.<br /> <br /> Now, while Im not saying that having any particular faith is incompatible with a scientific paradigm IN REAL LIFE, that does NOT coincide with the interests of a pure, mechanic materialistic worldview that the Union tries to impose.<br /> <br /> So, this holds true exclusively for the fictional universe of MtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T21:07:17-07:00","id":1491394,"title":"","content":"Science isn't the innate purview of any particular nation, culture or faith. History is written--and, sadly, often rewritten--by the victors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T23:35:04-07:00","id":1491396,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> I talk intimately to a lot of people across the world as part of my job and the idea that -science above religion- belongs to Europe alone (particularly the North and West) is a little laughable. Granted, I mostly talk to better-off people and it's statistically the poor that gets more religious, but the vibrancy of culture is pretty underwhelming and so I get a strong sense that most places would develop their own strong technocracy even if N/W Europe is ultimately more progressive and secular than them. Globalism is a pretty strong force even as it now declines in many ways. Even in countries that still have their own vibe going on, say, India, While I still got a couple of yogis the cultural difference Is less &quot;I'm religious and religion suggests X&quot; and more &quot;My whole family are engineers/Doctors/Lawyers/Computer scientists and like hell will anyone in my family choose another career&quot;: If that isn't going to breed technocrats, I'm not sure what will, and India is the <i>most </i>interesting example. Most everywhere else culture bows before modern living and religion/food/language/manners/friendliness aren't stopping people from embracing a world of science, at least with people that can afford to waste a little money on my services. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491383#post1491383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the advent of the scientific method - aka &quot;science&quot; - came to be in Europe and not in the Middle East or the Kingdom of Congo or the Aztec Empire or in China because of the particularities of christianism. For Islam for instance, everything is just simply the &quot;will of Allah&quot;, therefore it doesnt make sense to try to &quot;decypher&quot; the universe if things are just simply whatever Allah wills it to be at any given moment..</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just wrong. Muslim scholars also sought &quot;to understand God's creation&quot;. That's part of why they were scientifically well ahead around the time of the first millenium (the other reason being that they'd taken over all the christian learning centers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T00:45:43-07:00","id":1491400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491383#post1491383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the advent of the scientific method - aka &quot;science&quot; - came to be in Europe and not in the Middle East or the Kingdom of Congo or the Aztec Empire or in China because of the particularities of christianism. For Islam for instance, everything is just simply the &quot;will of Allah&quot;, therefore it doesnt make sense to try to &quot;decypher&quot; the universe if things are just simply whatever Allah wills it to be at any given moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree with this. Rational thought and empiricism which would later develop into the formalized scientific method are far older and widespread, and the method has been there in one form or another for thousands of years. Look up Ibn al-Haytham (Al-Hazen) for a particular good example of an early pioneer of the method in the middle east, but you can go back as far as the ancient world and find examples. This also holds true within the MtA universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491383#post1491383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The birth of science therefore, arose as an attempt to better understand &quot;God's mind&quot; - a fact that my fellow atheists sadly disregard (and even worse, ridicule on many occasions).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Faith in a creator deity or deities has always been a good motivator for exploring the wonders of their creation, the schism between science and religion is something that fundamentalists on either side perpetuated. The schism between the two and magic too, by the way. Albertus Magnus was a monk, scientist, and magician, and neither ecclesiastical nor secular contemporaries had any problems with that. There are many, many examples in other cultures for this as well- it was the norm for a long time that 'learned men' were members of their respective church because it gave them access to books and the time to study.<br /> Both the fusion of science, magic, religion, and art as well as their schism are global phenomena, and not limited to christian Europe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491383#post1491383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wont be able to remember where I read it - Guide to the Technocracy, I dont know. But it did indeed have entries for agents who were believers of some faith - mostly christianism or islam, but also buddism, hinduism and others, and it said that, althought the Technocratic official policy was that of quiet tolerance (aka it's fine as long as you dont proselitize), the entry also stated that those were often ridiculed by their colleages.<br /> <br /> Now, while Im not saying that having any particular faith is incompatible with a scientific paradigm IN REAL LIFE, that does NOT coincide with the interests of a pure, mechanic materialistic worldview that the Union tries to impose.<br /> <br /> So, this holds true exclusively for the fictional universe of MtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the Technocracy would only have problems with fundamentalists whose dogma interferes with their paradigm. &quot;Allah created everything including scientific principles&quot; still works while &quot;God powers my gun&quot; would be problematic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T01:57:03-07:00","id":1491405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491383#post1491383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the advent of the scientific method - aka &quot;science&quot; - came to be in Europe and not in the Middle East or the Kingdom of Congo or the Aztec Empire or in China because of the particularities of christianism. For Islam for instance, everything is just simply the &quot;will of Allah&quot;, therefore it doesnt make sense to try to &quot;decypher&quot; the universe if things are just simply whatever Allah wills it to be at any given moment.<br /> <br /> For Christianism however, the idea is that God created an understandable and RATIONAL world, which can be understood therefore using our reason.<br /> <br /> The birth of science therefore, arose as an attempt to better understand &quot;God's mind&quot; - a fact that my fellow atheists sadly disregard (and even worse, ridicule on many occasions).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to call poppycock on this. It has always been the purview of humanity to study and decipher the universe no matter where we were. Even Ancient Egypt and Babylon followed rational thought and the scientific method before the Greeks, Indians and Chinese codified it into their philosophies. For the most of history Christianity was very closeted off as far as science went and didn't encourage it outside proscribed circles, the ideals you espouse come into being with the Enlightenment period and only with the acts of the so called Enlightened monarchs driven by this interpretations to mass fund schools and scientific programs. And this only came because the primate of Church on knowledge was broken by the Renessiance and the printing press.<br /> <br /> And the contributions of Islamic scholars to the fields of chemistry, medicine, sailing, navigation and cartography are gigantic of the top of my head. I'm sure there's more I'm missing.<br /> <br /> Islamic, Indian, African and Chinese scholars contributed a lot to the body of knowledge and their ideas percolated through the world. I'm quite sure we'd have learned of more achievements and discoveries of subsaharan Africa and South America, were they not systematically overtaken and reeducated towards the &quot;right&quot; values.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T04:47:40-07:00","id":1491413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491344#post1491344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just point out, though, that the sleepers have not accepted the technocratic paradigm. If you look at World population, the vast majority of it is in Asia and Africa; North America is a relatively small percentage. To think that the essentially Western technocracy defines the consensus is its own little bit of hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, other areas of the world such as China, Japan and India have their own factions that are allied with the Technocracy or are sub-groups within the Technocracy (Zaibatsu, Five Metal Dragons, etc.) As a result the Technocracy is worldwide in scope. There are areas of the world, a few parts of South America, Africa and Southeast Asia where the Technocracy does not yet have an absolute stranglehold on local paradigms, but most of humanity is born into countries that fall under the Technocracy's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T07:31:41-07:00","id":1491418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491394#post1491394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science isn't the innate purview of any particular nation, culture or faith. History is written--and, sadly, often rewritten--by the victors</div> </div> </div> </div>When we talk about &quot;Science&quot; we mean the <u>Scientific Method</u>, because that's the most reliable tool to analyze the natural world. Scientific knowledge isnt the be all end all scope of human knowledge, the Scientific Method itself is anchored in philosophical insight, there are many things that fall outside of Science, like questions on morality, subjectivity and the sublime or mathmatical knowledge, which fall under the control of philosophy or logic, and I agree that for all of those there have been numerous nations and civilizations that have given unvaluable contributions, however the specific advent of the Scientific Method was invented solely by european christians. Later on it were adopted and expanded by everybody, sure, but the simple and undeniable fact is that it were first invented and used by the European Christendom, and the reasons for it is what I explained, for Christianism God created a rational and understandable world, which is a rather unique teological worldview when compared to pretty much any other religion in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T07:51:12-07:00","id":1491419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491418#post1491418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When we talk about &quot;Science&quot; we mean the <u>Scientific Method</u>, because that's the most reliable tool to analyze the natural world. Scientific knowledge isnt the be all end all scope of human knowledge, the Scientific Method itself is anchored in philosophical insight, there are many things that fall outside of Science, like questions on morality, subjectivity and the sublime or mathmatical knowledge, which fall under the control of philosophy or logic, and I agree that for all of those there have been numerous nations and civilizations that have given unvaluable contributions, however the specific advent of the Scientific Method was invented solely by european christians. Later on it were adopted and expanded by everybody, sure, but the simple and undeniable fact is that it were first invented and used by the European Christendom, and the reasons for it is what I explained, for Christianism God created a rational and understandable world, which is a rather unique teological worldview when compared to pretty much any other religion in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_scientific_method\" target=\"_blank\">Bullshit.</a> You're denying a minimum of 20 centuries of science by limiting it to a <i>short</i> period in which it was codified and organised by European thinkers who organised it into the modern academical structures.The Scientific Method has been around ever since someone wanted to systematically prove something and record this knowledge for analysys and later use. I got no idea where you got your schooling, but it's patently wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 08-26-2022, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T08:04:04-07:00","id":1491421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The New Atlantis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second caution about \u201cArabic science\u201d is that it was not science as we are familiar with it today. Pre-modern science, while not blind to utility, sought knowledge primarily in order to understand philosophical questions concerned with meaning, being, the good, and so on. Modern science, by contrast, grew out of a revolution in thought that reoriented politics around individual comfort through the mastery of nature. Modern science dismisses ancient metaphysical questions as (to borrow Francis Bacon\u2019s words) the pursuit of pleasure and vanity. Whatever modern science owes to Arabic science, the intellectual activity of the medieval Islamic world was not of the same kind as the European scientific revolution, which came after a radical break from ancient natural philosophy. Indeed, even though we use the term \u201cscience\u201d for convenience, it is important to remember that this word was not coined until the nineteenth century; the closest word in Arabic \u2014 ilm \u2014 means \u201cknowledge,\u201d and not necessarily that of the natural world.</div> </div> </div> </div>- &quot;Why the Arabic World Turned Away from Science - <br /> On the lost Golden Age and the rejection of reason&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.thenewatlantis.com/publications/why-the-arabic-world-turned-away-from-science\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.thenewatlantis.com/publi...y-from-science</a><br /> <br /> The islamic Golden Age did produced a massive plethora of accumulated knowledge, which both compiled knowledge previously developed by others, like Greeks, Romans, Egyptians, Persians, Indians and Chinese, but also developed on top of those.<br /> <br /> Likewise, many civilizations developed extensive amounts of human knowledge over the centuries, China, India, Egypt, Greece, Rome, Carthage, Persians.<br /> <br /> Despite many of those being a proto scientific creations, NONE of those were a representation of the modern day scientific revolution. There is a peculiarity that differentiates modern science from medieval or ancient knowledge, which aint just a mere formality. This is an important distinction to be made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The New Atlantis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arrival of paper also helped improve literacy, which had been encouraged since the dawn of Islam due to the religion\u2019s literary foundation, the Koran. Medieval Muslims took religious scholarship very seriously, and some scientists in the region grew up studying it. Avicenna, for example, is said to have known the entire Koran by heart before he arrived at Baghdad. Might it be fair, then, to say that Islam itself encouraged scientific enterprise? This question provokes wildly divergent answers. Some scholars argue that there are many parts of the Koran and the hadith (the sayings of Muhammad) that exhort believers to think about and try to understand Allah\u2019s creations in a scientific spirit. As one hadith urges, \u201cSeek knowledge, even in China.\u201d But there are other scholars who argue that \u201cknowledge\u201d in the Koranic sense is not scientific knowledge but religious knowledge, and that to conflate such knowledge with modern science is inaccurate and even na\u00efve</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-26-2022, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T08:20:37-07:00","id":1491422,"title":"","content":"Yes. And? How does any of that match your statement that the Scientific Method is a superior tool created by the European Christian scientist?<br /> <br /> Because right now you're moving the goalpost, and I specifically noted the difference in the later codification of knowledge into the modern scientific system and the emergence of a broad set of people able to work in science and share their ideas during the Enlightenment period. And since we know your history may be sketchy, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Enlightenment\" target=\"_blank\">Enlightenment is this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T10:48:32-07:00","id":1491429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491421#post1491421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.thenewatlantis.com/publications/why-the-arabic-world-turned-away-from-science\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.thenewatlantis.com/publi...y-from-science</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a politically motivated article, published in a journal that is not peer-reviewed for the sole reason of publishing politically biased articles. For such a publication to make statements what counts as science and what doesn't is.. rich.<br /> The article is contradictory at times, full of weasel-words, and willfully conflating different sociopolitcal mechanisms to paint a certain picture.<br /> <br /> But this serves as a good example on how politics can influence scientific consensus (and capital C Consensus). The Enlightenment was also a political movement. Political ideologies (independently of whether they are religiously motivated or not) have a massive influence on the public awareness and acceptance of science. Governments are able to influence the apparent importance of select scientific areas with funding, policies, and propaganda to create an environment that is more suitable to their agendas. It is a fallacy to think that science is science regardless of ideological environment- while scientific truth does not change, politics have a massive impact on how it is interpreted and implemented.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T11:13:31-07:00","id":1491432,"title":"","content":"The forum rules state we must respect others preferences, and the Mod has spoken for them, so I suppose that carries on even if those preferences are demonstrably wrong, dangerous and harmful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T15:07:52-07:00","id":1491441,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to be specific here in case Kakost keeps hanging on the method itself..<br /> <br /> Kakost invoked the Scientific Method as a delineation between science and not-science, which is preposterous. If he was just arguing that the exact concept of <i>&quot;Anything I cannot prove is outside of the scope of natural science&quot;</i> in the context of Science, he'd be roughly correct that it did arrive from the 17th and 18th Century and from the thought of the scientists of Enlightenment. Of course the concept of replicability and experiment based methodology which is the foundation of the Scientific Method was a part of the exact Golden Age of Islamic science his article mentions.<br /> <br /> However, that ONLY applies only to natural sciences. And ironically those would not exist without philosophy, something hard pressed to actual adhere to the scientific method. One thing that especially galls me here is that this approach is not founded in the thesis of <i>&quot;God made a rational world&quot;</i> but in <i>&quot;I cannot prove that God exists, therefore it's none of my business&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Denying the scientific achievements and technological advancements of the world before Enlightenment is insulting to the history and ingenuity of mankind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T16:12:35-07:00","id":1491442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491383#post1491383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Islam for instance, everything is just simply the &quot;will of Allah&quot;, therefore it doesnt make sense to try to &quot;decypher&quot; the universe if things are just simply whatever Allah wills it to be at any given moment.<br /> <br /> For Christianism however, the idea is that God created an understandable and RATIONAL world, which can be understood therefore using our reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to add to what everyone is already saying:<br /> <br /> The Quran itself has several passages directly commanding scholars to study God's creation, it is considered <u>extremely</u> important that the Faithful have scientists among them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, while the Catholic Church <b>did</b> had interest in scientific development for most of its history, and many Christian priests defended that Creation was fundamentally rational, this has <b>never</b> been its basis. On the contrary, blind faith is usually seen as a virtue, while the Quran commands the Faithful to be always studious.<br /> <br /> I have read both the Bible and the Quran, despite not following either. I am very picky about my sources and their sources, and usually take care into comparing sources with distinct bias to see how they agree and disagree. I'll take a look at this TNA, but in this regard it is going against not only a huge number of independent sources, but literally against the primary sources, attributing to them things they verifiably don't say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T06:57:01-07:00","id":1491468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491442#post1491442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to add to what everyone is already saying:<br /> <br /> The Quran itself has several passages directly commanding scholars to study God's creation, it is considered <u>extremely</u> important that the Faithful have scientists among them.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, while the Catholic Church <b>did</b> had interest in scientific development for most of its history, and many Christian priests defended that Creation was fundamentally rational, this has <b>never</b> been its basis. On the contrary, blind faith is usually seen as a virtue, while the Quran commands the Faithful to be always studious.<br /> <br /> I have read both the Bible and the Quran, despite not following either. I am very picky about my sources and their sources, and usually take care into comparing sources with distinct bias to see how they agree and disagree. I'll take a look at this TNA, but in this regard it is going against not only a huge number of independent sources, but literally against the primary sources, attributing to them things they verifiably don't say.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've stated multiple times, Im an atheist, but not only that, Im an skeptical materialist. So to me, the Bible, Quran, Illyad, the Eddas or the Mahabharata are all equally mythological, just like Zeus and what not.<br /> <br /> Im not here to have theological debates, I dont care about that. But I do care about truth. And the truth is:<br /> <br /> - Islam had a Golden Age, upon which, like all civilizations, they took the knowledge of anothers and expanded upon it, drinking from the greeks, romans, egyptians, persians and indians. During that time, Islamic civilization was the candle of light of knowledge in humanity.<br /> <br /> - Europe meanwhile was in a mud of theocratic fundamentalism. Gone was all the knowledge of the Greeks, Romans and Egyptians in Europe. Luckly, all of that was preserved by the muslims, and in time those would return to Europe, and on top of that even more knowledge that the muslims incorporated from Persia and India and that which the muslims created themselves.<br /> <br /> - The islamic civilization sunk into theocratic fundamentalism. Libraries and books began to be burned. Meanwhile, religious fundamentalism in Europe began to recede, giving birth to the Renascence and the Enlightment.<br /> <br /> The loss of &quot;love&quot; for knowledge is NOT uncommon. Civilizations rise and fall; in their period of ascension, in the Spring and Summer of a nation, the body of knowledge that they create blossoms, but at their decline, it all decays. This happened in Europe too - SEVERAL times. Before the Greeks, there were the Minoan civilization, who were on par with the Egyptians, Babylonians and Persians. But then comes the Bronze Age Collapse, and ALL of their achievements were gone FOR GOOD. We know very little about them. What we call the &quot;classic&quot; greeks is in fact the &quot;post-apocaliptic&quot; civilization that came out from the ashes of the minoans, and whatever knowledge they had was mostly lost - forever.<br /> <br /> During the decline of Rome, the same thing happened. The knowledge for roman aqueducts, for example, was lost forever. Roman roads remained the best all the way up to the 19th century. This decline in knowledge actually happened before the final dissolution of the SQPR. Over the last centuries of the roman empire, their architecture had already decayed, their military prowess was long gone - and by that I dont mean number of manpower, but technical skills of their military and tactics development.<br /> <br /> There is something unique that developed in Europe, from the 17th century towards the 19th, which today is called the &quot;Scientific Revolution&quot;. And, unlike what seems to be a historical rule, it didnt go away - at least so far.<br /> <br /> But there's a reason for this. First of all, the modern Scientific Revolution coincided with the Industrial Revolution, and one improves upon the other.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the world became much more connected than in the past. Before the Great Navigations, the Roman decline was a non issue for China. The collapse of any single chinese dinasty had no impact whatsoever in North Africa.<br /> <br /> The first time knowledge was spread in large scale between civilizations was during Alexander's expansion. That connected Greece (which were basically the only thing Europe had, with the exception of an infant Etruscan civilization in Italy that would spawn Rome) with Persia, Egypt and India, leaving only China outside from this massive exchange.<br /> <br /> That however, would not be replicated again until the islamic Golden Age from roughly the 8th century to the 14th, once again connecting India all the way to Greece.<br /> <br /> After the Great Navigations however, the world became interconnected. Europe could face a total collapse and civilizational dissolution, and the rest of the world would continue to push foward with the Scientific Revolution. Japan for example fully embraced the Scientific and Industrial Revolutions during the Meiji Restoration.<br /> <br /> In fact, nowadays Europe aint even the major center of scientific development: the US is, with China and Japan also becoming important centers (althought I believe China is doomed and will utterly collapse soon). And India is on a huge rise, and I believe India (not China) may soon become the &quot;New Mecca&quot; of the world.<br /> <br /> Other than all of that, the modern Scientific Revolution is different from everything that existed before. Philosophy exists since antiguity, and a huge amount of knowledge accumulated, none of that had the formality of the Scientific Method, and the philosophical principles of the Scientific Method had not had been formulated. This is important, and not just a petty nitpicking. The lack of a Scientific Method is what allowed Plato to remain unchallenged for centuries in the idea that everything is made off Earth, Fire, Air and Water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T07:26:53-07:00","id":1491472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491441#post1491441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to be specific here in case Kakost keeps hanging on the method itself..<br /> <br /> Kakost invoked the Scientific Method as a delineation between science and not-science, which is preposterous. If he was just arguing that the exact concept of <i>&amp;quot;Anything I cannot prove is outside of the scope of natural science&amp;quot;</i> in the context of Science, he'd be roughly correct that it did arrive from the 17th and 18th Century and from the thought of the scientists of Enlightenment. Of course the concept of replicability and experiment based methodology which is the foundation of the Scientific Method was a part of the exact Golden Age of Islamic science his article mentions.<br /> <br /> However, that ONLY applies only to natural sciences. And ironically those would not exist without philosophy, something hard pressed to actual adhere to the scientific method. One thing that especially galls me here is that this approach is not founded in the thesis of <i>&amp;quot;God made a rational world&amp;quot;</i> but in <i>&amp;quot;I cannot prove that God exists, therefore it's none of my business&amp;quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Denying the scientific achievements and technological advancements of the world before Enlightenment is insulting to the history and ingenuity of mankind.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are answering questions I did not make. I believe that if you move to some of my previous posts, you'll find that I explicitly said that &quot;Science&quot;, or more specifically, the Scientific Method, does not and can not resume the entirety of human knowledge. Heck, the Scientific Method cannot prove the Scientific Method.<br /> <br /> The Scientific Method is a philosophical tool; it's the discipline of philosophy and logic that anchors it's utility as the best tool to understand and codify the natural world.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Scientific Method uses several other tools that fall outside of its purview, the most important of which being Math, which is a discipline of Logic.<br /> <br /> And there are many other disciplines that not necessarily follows the Scientific Method or are purely descriptive. For example, a lot of historical knowledge is purely descriptive. There are still some elements of the Scientific Method into it, particularly for historical research, but most of it is descriptive rather than experimental.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I never said that &quot;there were no advances before Enlightment&quot;. Once again, you are answering a question I never made. What my point was is that the advent of the Scientific Method created a formalized way of analyzing knowledge in a trustworthy way, which is unique in human history. This funtamental difference is what finally allowed humanity to dismiss ideas such as the 4 bodily humours and develop the germ theory among others.<br /> <br /> That represents a fundamental cornerstone into the Consensus that isnt just a footnote detail.<br /> <br /> As for the role of &quot;God&quot; into all of this, God is only taken out of the picture from the 19th century onward. Before that, everything was divine - and the pursue of knowledge was a literal pursue of the divine. <br /> <br /> Now, as everything about theology, interpretations change over time. The Quran praised knowledge - initially - and that brought the Islamic Golden Age. But, when that interpretation from &quot;you must seek knowledge&quot; to &quot;you must ONLY seek knowledge related to Islam&quot; due to political changes in the islamic civilization, that golden age ended and religious zealotry sunk in. Likewise, when the christian doctrine changed from &quot;heretic and heathen knowledge is dangerous&quot; to &quot;knowledge is Divine&quot;, it began their own Golden Age","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T10:20:52-07:00","id":1491492,"title":"","content":"Wherever sleepers go, Mages follow. Since the Union is the cultural echo of north american capitalist normativity, you'll see typical western cultural values reflected in how the Union operates. Since every Mage is a precious resource, heteronormative oppression won't take place in official policy. It will take place in the same way that it does in corporate America - passing over for promotions, mission assignment and career opportunities. Even if things like transphobia and racism are officially decried as &quot;unmutual&quot;, victimization will continue to take place because Technocratic culture is an echo of the same imperialist, colonialist culture that created it. Further, people don't forget their sleeper values - if you were a dedicated white evangelical christian who held certain views and then you were recruited into the Technocracy, I don't think those would change<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","user":"Robert Armsley","date":". 08-27-2022, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:25:37-07:00","id":1491501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491468#post1491468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've stated multiple times, Im an atheist, but not only that, Im an skeptical materialist. So to me, the Bible, Quran, Illyad, the Eddas or the Mahabharata are all equally mythological, just like Zeus and what not.<br /> <br /> Im not here to have theological debates, I dont care about that. But I do care about truth. And the truth is:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not supporting any religion (I directly stated I don't follow them) or having theological debates.<br /> <br /> The truth is that you <b>directly stated</b> that Christianity had a belief in reason <i>as a core principle </i>and Islam was the opposite. <b><u>This is false</u> </b>and in no uncertain terms. You <b>explicitly</b> said that this distinction in core belief was a component to their distinct directions in development towards or against the scientific method, but this distinction is a patently false assumption.<br /> <br /> And I'm not talking about any other aspect of your analysis and arguments. I'm not interested in the rest of the discussion for several reasons, chief among them that I have little to add, others already said anything else I would and I'm not going to just add volume here (I currently have to pick my debates because time is constrained).<br /> <br /> However your opinion on religion is, you can't use it as an excuse to make assertions about religion, but then excuse yourself from their criticism. True or not as descriptions of reality, religions are concrete aspects of human culture and must be taken as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T07:45:47-07:00","id":1491591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491501#post1491501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not supporting any religion (I directly stated I don't follow them) or having theological debates.<br /> <br /> The truth is that you <b>directly stated</b> that Christianity had a belief in reason <i>as a core principle </i>and Islam was the opposite. <b><u>This is false</u> </b>and in no uncertain terms. You <b>explicitly</b> said that this distinction in core belief was a component to their distinct directions in development towards or against the scientific method, but this distinction is a patently false assumption.<br /> <br /> And I'm not talking about any other aspect of your analysis and arguments. I'm not interested in the rest of the discussion for several reasons, chief among them that I have little to add, others already said anything else I would and I'm not going to just add volume here (I currently have to pick my debates because time is constrained).<br /> <br /> However your opinion on religion is, you can't use it as an excuse to make assertions about religion, but then excuse yourself from their criticism. True or not as descriptions of reality, religions are concrete aspects of human culture and must be taken as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well. So let me rectify myself. Religious interpretations change over time, and as such those have been inverted from both Christianity and Islam. Mostly by the decline of the Abbasid Caliphate, which plunged Islam into an obscurantist interpretation of the Quran. Meanwhile, in Europe the reduction of the power of the Catholic church with both the centralization of power with monarchs but even more importantly, the protestant revolution and the religious wars, brought an end to the medieval european obscurantism and new interpretations to christianism.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it's still a matter of theology causing societal changes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T08:38:27-07:00","id":1491601,"title":"","content":"Except the Renaissance began well before the protestant reformation<br /> Europe advanced largely because it was ruled by warriors and thus <i>constantly</i> at war with itself (and with leaders much more personally invested in getting results than what was typical in more peaceable places). For a very obvious example look at how armour changed between 900 and 1500. These many improvements were difficult and expensive, and in turn brought about new ways to organize business and finance wars. This strengthened the merchant class, and by the renaissance the warrior elite were in trouble because a man with a life of training + personal equipment that costs more than a few villages isn't much better militarily than Jeff who spent two weeks learning how to use a musket. So the merchants started gaining ground and competing and eventually rather than merchants supporting warriors you get things like the VOC and EIC, the closest things we've actually had to Anarcho-Capitalism, so you <i>should</i> know about this. But I suppose most don't become self-described right wing extremists actually knowing what their ideology results in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-28-2022, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:42:55-07:00","id":1491611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491601#post1491601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Renaissance began well before the protestant reformation<br /> Europe advanced largely because it was ruled by warriors and thus <i>constantly</i> at war with itself (and with leaders much more personally invested in getting results than what was typical in more peaceable places). For a very obvious example look at how armour changed between 900 and 1500. These many improvements were difficult and expensive, and in turn brought about new ways to organize business and finance wars. This strengthened the merchant class, and by the renaissance the warrior elite were in trouble because a man with a life of training + personal equipment that costs more than a few villages isn't much better militarily than Jeff who spent two weeks learning how to use a musket. So the merchants started gaining ground and competing and eventually rather than merchants supporting warriors you get things like the VOC and EIC, the closest things we've actually had to Anarcho-Capitalism, so you <i>should</i> know about this. But I suppose most don't become self-described right wing extremists actually knowing what their ideology results in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Renaissance began in Italy due to the trade between the Italian city states with the middle eastern/north african caliphates and the ottoman sultanate, which did exactly the movement of reintroducing the greek and roman knowledge that had been lost in Europe but were preserved and expanded by the arabs, back to Europe.<br /> <br /> At the same time thou, you have a series of changes in canonical laws and theological interpretations that would set the terrain for the future scientific revolution.<br /> <br /> The Protestant Revolution represents the end point of a movement that begun long before - just like everything in history, it's a continuum of actions. The church of St. Peter and the first christian martyrs being shredded to pieces by the Romans is NOT the same church as the one institutionalized by the emperor Constantine, nor is it the same as during the schism between Catholics and Orthodoxes. Likewise, the Islam of today aint the same Islam of Mohammed, not the same Islam left after the death of Ali and the schism of Sunni and Shia, nor the same of the Abassid Caliphate or the Ottoman Sultanate.<br /> <br /> Believe it or not, theological dogma changes according to the political needs of the moment. Yeah, crazy, I know.<br /> <br /> As to your preconceptions about anarcho capitalism, this is neither the place nor the time. I just want to point out how unnecessarily hateful you are sounding towards something you dont really understand and towards someone who have not attacked you. Your personal attacks towards me speak against yourself alone, not against me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:44:04-07:00","id":1491613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491601#post1491601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Renaissance began well before the protestant reformationBut I suppose most don't become self-described right wing extremists actually knowing what their ideology results in.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Personal insults. Out of this thread.<br /> <br /> Take an infraction.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:58:31-07:00","id":1491618,"title":"","content":"Yes yes, Fascists are bad because they hate specific people. Anarcho capitalists are fine because they hate everyone equally. Making laws to screw people is bad, but removing laws that protect people is a perfectly healthy political stance. No. It's not. Go on, enjoy your opiates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Believe it or not, theological dogma changes according to the political needs of the moment. Yeah, crazy, I know. </div> </div> </div>Theological dogma changing according to the political needs of the moment supports the idea that theological dogma doesn't fucking matter and there's next to nothing about being Christian gave Europe an advantage, at least compared to geography, technology, politics, culture. Arguments like this are why man-portable rocket launchers have &quot;This way towards enemy&quot; painted on them. While the christianization of europe had it's perks, it certainly wasn't <i>the</i> factor that led to the scientific paradigm and the overwhelming european dominance of the 17th-20th centuries.<br /> <br /> (edit: Wrote this without seeing the red. If only I wrote faster)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-28-2022, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T10:36:08-07:00","id":1491621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491432#post1491432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forum rules state we must respect others preferences, and the Mod has spoken for them, so I suppose that carries on even if those preferences are demonstrably wrong, dangerous and harmful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasnt going to adress this, but since you decided to turn a discussion that so far had been an &quot;academical&quot; one into a personal attack, I think I will oblige:<br /> <br /> 1 - Passive-agressive demeanor. You are not saying it, because you know that it isnt allowed, but when you saying &quot;wrong or dangerous&quot;, you are using a <i>Reductio ad Hitlerum</i>, or in other words, instead of trying to beat my arguments, you seek to imply that Im a fascist or a nazist - a very typical recourse from one specific side of the political spectrum that is used to disqualify a person and thus shut down debate. <br /> <br /> 2 - This becomes evident by your vitriolic use of &quot;far right&quot; in your last post to further disqualify me on a personal level, seeking to add togheter perceived notions of what is considered to be a &quot;far right extremist&quot; - speaking very clearly, the game here is to always associate &quot;far right&quot; with &quot;nazi&quot;.<br /> <br /> 3 - and in this, you once again show your complete lack of proper knowledge of what Anarcho-Capitalism is, since the Libertarian political spectrum, althought having <i>some</i> points in common with what is considered to be &quot;typical&quot; right wing's points, is also unique. For example, Im an atheist and a strict adherent to secularism and absolute religious freedom, while right wingers are typically religious conservatives. Conservatives are also advocates of a paternalistic State that would upkeep &quot;the morals of society&quot;, while Libertarians (from which Ancaps are a subgroup contained within) want the State completely removed from interfering in the personal lives of people. One good example of which is the legalization of drugs: Conservatives believe that the State should forcibly coherce people not to consume narcotics, while Libertarians such as myself believe in &quot;F* the State!&quot;. Also, Conservatives are anti-abortion, while that is not a settled thing amongst Libertarians (some are pro abortion, some against).<br /> Another example is gay marriage, with Conservatives being mostly against, while Libertarians believe that actions of individuals, such as marriage, shouldnt even need the &quot;blessing&quot; of the State to begin with.<br /> Instead of making gay marriage &quot;legal&quot;, take the bureocrats out of my home and my dinner table, how about that? I dont need nor require &quot;permission&quot; from daddy State to associate myself with anybody I so wish.<br /> <br /> In fact, the left Progressives have far more in common with right wing Conservatives than Libertarians do, since Progressives too believe that the State should have a role in meddling into the lives of the citizens. In this point, both the leftist Progressives and the Conservatives right wingers share common ground. It's no wonder that, in the end, both Fascism and Socialism (the two political sides taken to their extremes) look so much alike.<br /> <br /> 4 - Insinuating that an Ancap is a &quot;fascist&quot; (with your passive-agressive insinuations) is the final revelation that you do not know what you are criticizing. There are many <u>valid</u> criticisms towards Libertarianism in general or Anarcho-Capitalism in particular that would be completely fine to be done, and althought I believe in what I believe, I do not think that any idea should be above scrutiny, therefore whatever criticisms you may have towards it are absolutely valid; but that's NOT what you did. You're NOT attacking the ideas of Anarcho-Capitalism, but rather you're creating a strawman and attacking that. Nazifascism, as well as Socialism, represent total control of the State over every aspects of society - aka totalitarianism.<br /> <br /> Anarcho-Capitalism, as well as the other variations of Anarchism (mostly &quot;Classic Anarchism&quot; or Anarcho-Communism, to which I have many ideological allergies towards but hey, they at least are anarchists too) is as far from totalitarianism as it's possible to get; your own political ideology, be it as it may, is closer to fascism than mine, by definition.<br /> <br /> 5 - <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The forum rules state we must respect others preferences... even if those preferences are demonstrably wrong, dangerous and <b>harmful.</b> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely revealing. It shows that, should it have it your way, you would just simply shut down anyone that thinks in a way that you dont approve off. This is a sign of authoritarianism. I'd be careful if I were you, brother, because this is the EXACT path taken by all those ideas that you claim to oppose.<br /> <br /> This also proves EXACTLY my previous points when I were talking about Mages positioning themselves as the moral authorities and becoming tyrants, because that's EXACTLY what you're doing. You're placing yourself in the position of judge of what right and wrong is, and that you're the &quot;enlightned&quot; soul that is fit for the job. I dont mean it as a personal attack, but I would rather want to invite you to reflect about it. Because this is the very same dark path that is used on all the great atrocities in human history - from the Crusades, Inquisition and Jihad to the horrors of the French Revolution, WW2 and communism, all of those were perpetrated by people who believed themselves to be doing things for the &quot;greater good&quot;. Just think about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-28-2022, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T16:32:46-07:00","id":1491673,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> I have this feeling that you're so caught up in trying to prove how well read you are that you've missed the forest for the trees. You can keep whatever views you want as long as you don't hurt anyone else by practising them, which you've already spoken at length about in the earlier discussion of the moral burden of the Mage. The problem is that you espoused a set of views that focused on a reductionist eurocentric view that neither gelled with the spirit of scientific achievement nor with the fact that the contributions and history of science are varied and quite more broad then presented. The whole marriage of God with the Scientific Method did not help (because face it, you know that Deism is but a waypoint on the road to the Scientific Method). You probably didn't mean it like it sounded, but it ended up interpreted like that.<br /> <br /> After all, we don't know how differently history would have unfolded with slightly different geopolitical and societal pressures. Europe happened to be in a place where it was rich, driven by a need for advancement and a lack of scruples about using it. Considering that history is just one set of variables and you being unable to experimentally prove that the same results couldn't be reproduced with a different set of variables, you may have to settle on the fact that there could have been other way for things to unfold and still end similar to where we are now.<br /> <br /> Now that we've gone through what antagonised a part of the forum, would you kindly get back to the topic? If you want to discuss the impacts of anarcho-capitalism in Mage and which paradigms and factions would support it, that's a solid topic. But let's stop this logorhoea under this topic as you're not going to change minds like this. At the end of the day people will pick their own reality and live with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T16:45:49-07:00","id":1491678,"title":"","content":"Yes. Could we please talk about sex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:02:30-07:00","id":1491679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491678#post1491678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Could we please talk about sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's talk about sex, baybeee...<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm quite intrigued by the Syndicate's approach. Considering their general outlook I doubt the power dynamics thing is fully consensual and I wonder how they keep things from exploding horribly. However, I can totally see them providing all kinds of sexual services and organising all kinds of content to get their hooks into the other Conventions. Ars Cupidae at its best!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:07:49-07:00","id":1491680,"title":"","content":"So, on topic, according to Technocracy Reloaded that I got around to finishing from among my reading backlog. They are completely supportive of people across the spectrum of gender identity, including the gender fluid and non-binary. There are of course hold outs that are against it but official policy is that they go so far to offer hyper tech transition procedures as an employee perk and don't discriminate. Procreation and interpersonal relationships are tightly controlled, you have to file paperwork and get permission and such for them from your superiors if you want to get into a personal relationship and have kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:21:44-07:00","id":1491685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491680#post1491680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, on topic, according to Technocracy Reloaded that I got around to finishing from among my reading backlog. They are completely supportive of people across the spectrum of gender identity, including the gender fluid and non-binary. There are of course hold outs that are against it but official policy is that they go so far to offer hyper tech transition procedures as an employee perk and don't discriminate. Procreation and interpersonal relationships are tightly controlled, you have to file paperwork and get permission and such for them from your superiors if you want to get into a personal relationship and have kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I did apretty long writeup on it... 6 pages ago &lt;facepalm&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my copy of Technocracy Reloaded spent quite a while in limbo and the physical one still isn't with me as I sent it to a buddy rather then to myself. This thread made me take a look at the pdf. There is actually quite a bit of text in the book about what the Technocracy thinks of sex, relationships and gender identity:<ul><li>Technocracy realised they had an issue with toxic masculinity from 1900s to1980s</li> <li>Chauvinism and machismo were seen as unproductive and wasteful and efforts were made to correct it</li> <li>No restrictions on sexual preferences or gender identity</li> <li>Only effective operatives are the ones who are comfortable with their identity, therefore technocracy offers hypertech gender-affirmation surgery to help their members with issues</li> <li>The former is actually seen as decadent and corrupt by certain Traditions</li> <li>Sexual preference stigmas are officially forbidden in the Technocracy</li> <li>There may be certain situations where the Technocracy restricts who you can be with (cowerkers, special mission types)</li> <li>Birth control and STD prevention/control for all</li> <li>Having children is limited by requiring a certain rank in the Technocracy</li> <li>Citizens have no limitations on having kids, meaning that low level mages are the ones most impacted by this</li> <li>All the above stuff - treatment, birth control and gender-reaffirming procedures - are available to the Citizens! &quot;Happy healthy, satisfied workforce tends to be an extremely loyal workforce&quot;</li> <li>Stigma and harsh punishments for any form of sexual violence</li> <li>Children are a priority and anyone in Technocracy is expected to educate and help with them</li> <li>Cannot date direct superiors or direct subordinates, harsh consequences</li> <li>If the other side is eligible, relationship status needs to be reported, and no sex before paperwork</li> <li>Sex =/= Relationship</li> <li>Sex and polyamoury are quite common, especially in Iteration X and NWO</li> <li>So is asexuality - be it due to being processed, traumatized or not built for it, asexual people feel especially comfortable here</li> <li>Syndicate is sex crazed and tends to ignore rules about relationships (except rape), love of abusing power dynamics,sex is a weapon and domination is a mark of success, this makes other conventions wary of them</li> <li>Progenitors have a almost creepy fascination with the mechanics of procreation</li> <li>The Void Engineers are both geeky cosmonauts and the horniest technocrats alive (also sex with extradimensional beings can make men pregnant)</li> <li>Marriage is only allowed for high rank technocrats with high loyalty, no boundaries on gender, sexual identity or number of people you are married to</li> <li>You get to work with the people you are married to and usually get joint assignments</li> <li>Joint quarters and</li> <li>Married people get licenses for kids more easily, also parental leave</li> <li>Partnership is the &quot;simple&quot; variant of Marriage without the bureacracy, less concessions from Technocracy</li> <li>Divorce is handled by giving the sides involved separate quarters and a mediator to establish if there is any damage to the Technocracy, relationship counseling is offered if it can help, if not communal belongings are shared equally unless there are infractions or abuse, Children become wards of the Union (many Technocrats prefer to stay married for this reason)</li> </ul><br /> ... Yes, THAT IS A LOT OF WORDCOUNT if this is just a summary. Check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:24:31-07:00","id":1491686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491679#post1491679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's talk about sex, baybeee...<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm quite intrigued by the Syndicate's approach. Considering their general outlook I doubt the power dynamics thing is fully consensual and I wonder how they keep things from exploding horribly. However, I can totally see them providing all kinds of sexual services and organising all kinds of content to get their hooks into the other Conventions. Ars Cupidae at its best!</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things to remember is that the Syndics are the Technocratic Masters of Prime. As such, there are likely to be some parallels between their approach to sex and, e.g., Tantra. It's just not going to be phrased in terms of energy flows where the Syndicate is concerned.<br /> <br /> I would point out that is very easy to get it wrong with the Syndicate's approach; there's an entire faction of Nephandi who show just <i>how</i> wrong it can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-28-2022, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:40:15-07:00","id":1491687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491685#post1491685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I did apretty long writeup on it... 6 pages ago &lt;facepalm&gt;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really sure what you were expecting when you asked us to get back on topic in a topic whose original question was already answered. There is nothing else that can be said beyond redundant confirmation that 'yep, this is what Technocracy Reloaded says about gender identity and interpersonal relationships'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:48:25-07:00","id":1491690,"title":"","content":"Well, the initial discussion pretty much focused, not so much on sex was on LGBT issues. There were a few brief mentions of the act itself; but it was largely passed over. The main thing I remember about it is that there was a general assumption that the Union as a whole approaches out porky from a materialistic perspective, devoid of any greater metaphysical significance. <br /> <br /> As I implied in my last post, I think the Syndicate would be the biggest exception to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:54:55-07:00","id":1491692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491686#post1491686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the things to remember is that the Syndics are the Technocratic Masters of Prime. As such, there are likely to be some parallels between their approach to sex and, e.g., Tantra. It's just not going to be phrased in terms of energy flows where the Syndicate is concerned.<br /> <br /> I would point out that is very easy to get it wrong with the Syndicate's approach; there's an entire faction of Nephandi who show just <i>how</i> wrong it can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, you could actually power effects and gain quintessence from acts, and the bigger and more spectacular acts with more participants could do wonders and Wonders! What kind of Talismans are powered by a Syndicate orgy?<br /> <br /> The reason why I was curious about the thoughts on the Power Dynamics thing is that it seems like a slight mismatch. Technocracy is formally against patronisation where there may be power abuse and sanctions it strongly due to possible abuse or fallout. Syndicate members specifically enjoy messed up power dynamics which is counter this partyline. They seem to get away with it and have this whole &quot;my influence, my prerrogative who I fuck&quot;. That's bound to cause issues, tensions and problems within the Syndicate even before other Conventions interact with them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T18:22:00-07:00","id":1491696,"title":"","content":"Books about the Technocracy have a tendency to portray it all through the lens of the New World Order. For example, the talk in Technocracy Reloaded about what field agents in the Technocracy look and act like sounds suspiciously like what Black Hats would look and act like. The thing is, I have a hard time believing that any of the other Conventions would fall in line so readily. Well, maybe Iteration X. Maybe.<br /> <br /> But in many ways, The Syndicate is the polar opposite of the New World Order. There's a reason why the revised Convention Books talk about an upcoming Technocratic Civil War painted the New World Order and The Syndicate as the rival poles in that conflict. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I tend to agree that Syndicate power dynamics and NWO hierarchy don't mesh very well. That's not just a matter of sex; that's the whole ball of wax. <br /> <br /> While the worst of the Syndicate shows a callousness about the well-being of others, and shows just how damaging rampant selfishness can be, the more moderate Syndic is a potentially noble figure; a champion of individual rights. The New World Order, meanwhile, it's pretty much as far opposite in terms of individual rights and you can get. It would not surprise me in the least, for example, if the Syndicate had a secret deprogramming center, to keep their personnel free of NWO brainwashing. For an entirely different reason from why the Void Engineers do it, mind you; but the result would be about the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-29-2022, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T01:37:20-07:00","id":1491722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491692#post1491692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, you could actually power effects and gain quintessence from acts, and the bigger and more spectacular acts with more participants could do wonders and Wonders! What kind of Talismans are powered by a Syndicate orgy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's one: Say you control large chunks of the online pornography industry for commercial reasons already, and one day you overhear one of the geeks talking about distributed processing- suddenly you're looking at a large network of sleepers you can harvest as unknowing ritual participants for your next tantric session.<br /> <br /> Porn is probably also a good vector for subliminal messages and the like. It has a wide spread and psychologoically addictive properties, so it's maybe another contested sector between Syndicate and NWO.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T02:28:50-07:00","id":1491725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491696#post1491696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Books about the Technocracy have a tendency to portray it all through the lens of the New World Order. For example, the talk in Technocracy Reloaded about what field agents in the Technocracy look and act like sounds suspiciously like what Black Hats would look and act like. The thing is, I have a hard time believing that any of the other Conventions would fall in line so readily. Well, maybe Iteration X. Maybe.<br /> <br /> But in many ways, The Syndicate is the polar opposite of the New World Order. There's a reason why the revised Convention Books talk about an upcoming Technocratic Civil War painted the New World Order and The Syndicate as the rival poles in that conflict.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I tend to agree that Syndicate power dynamics and NWO hierarchy don't mesh very well. That's not just a matter of sex; that's the whole ball of wax.<br /> <br /> While the worst of the Syndicate shows a callousness about the well-being of others, and shows just how damaging rampant selfishness can be, the more moderate Syndic is a potentially noble figure; a champion of individual rights. The New World Order, meanwhile, it's pretty much as far opposite in terms of individual rights and you can get. It would not surprise me in the least, for example, if the Syndicate had a secret deprogramming center, to keep their personnel free of NWO brainwashing. For an entirely different reason from why the Void Engineers do it, mind you; but the result would be about the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never picked up the new convention books post ItX. Are they worth it? Does it cover this tension between the conventions well? Does it give something new and special to the factions that's worth a look? Also anything on Syndicate sex stuff? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491722#post1491722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one: Say you control large chunks of the online pornography industry for commercial reasons already, and one day you overhear one of the geeks talking about distributed processing- suddenly you're looking at a large network of sleepers you can harvest as unknowing ritual participants for your next tantric session.<br /> <br /> Porn is probably also a good vector for subliminal messages and the like. It has a wide spread and psychologoically addictive properties, so it's maybe another contested sector between Syndicate and NWO.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's how PornHub was made.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:11:56-07:00","id":1491737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491432#post1491432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forum rules state we must respect others preferences, and the Mod has spoken for them, so I suppose that carries on even if those preferences are demonstrably wrong, dangerous and harmful.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You could try reporting rather than openly insulting posters. You were warned yesterday about this and continued. Take a ban for three days.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T05:42:13-07:00","id":1491746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491725#post1491725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never picked up the new convention books post ItX. Are they worth it? Does it cover this tension between the conventions well? Does it give something new and special to the factions that's worth a look? Also anything on Syndicate sex stuff? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they had a <i>lot</i> of stuff that was new and special \u2014 which, for the most part, promptly got incorporated into M20. Remember: with the exception of the Iteration X book, the Revised Convention Books were actually produced a year before M20 was announced. <br /> <br /> NWO introduced the Data Sphere, and updated their gear to something more appropriate to the 21st century. It also introduced the ATLAS program, where the NWO took over Iteration X's now-defunct cyborg program (Iteration X had shifted its attention to Hardsuits) and was putting the brains of captured Awakened personnel into cyborg bodies. <br /> <br /> I don't recall much of what the Progenitors book did, other than to set them up as the Convention that was trying to heal the divide between three NWO and The Syndicate. That, and there was less emphasis on them as a source of body horror and more emphasis on them as <i>doctors</i>. <br /> <br /> The Syndicate book is where the concept of Primal Utility was introduced; before that, the most common perception of the Syndicate was that money magic centers around the probabilistic elements of Entropy. So that was a <i>big</i> new development \u2014 dare I say, a game changer. And for the first time that I'm aware of, the Syndicate paradigm was presented in a way that made sense, and wasn't a balancing act between \u201care they even Awakened?\u201d and \u201cAre they even Technocrats?\u201d I still go to that book for advice on how the Syndicate's Practice and Instruments work. <br /> <br /> The Void Engineers were completely reinvented: no longer peaceful explorers of the Umbra who were on the verge of abandoning the Technocracy, they were now space marines fighting a desperate war against a danger that their fellow Earthside Conventions were uniquely vulnerable to: Threat Null. Any notion of abandoning the Union was gone, because you don't abandon someone who is in so much danger. It also introduced Tychoidean Cosmology, a subject touched on in M20 but much more thoroughly explained in the Convention Book, as well as revising Dimensional Science from \u201cjust like Spirit, except that you can create portals to the Umbra inside Technocratic strongholds\u201d to a full-on variant Sphere that places more emphasis on Gauntlet Manipulation, less on Extra-Dimensional Entities, and what EDE focus remained shifted from binding and controlling them to fighting them: more Ghostbusters. There was also a <i>short</i> section on \u201cVoid Correspondence\u201d, which took the Correspondence Sphere in the opposite direction from what Data did to it, making it <i>more</i> about Space and less about mystical connections. Oh, and the Voidships. The VE Convention Book gives design rules for their spacecraft. <br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm glad I got all of them when they came out. In today's environment, I'd be less inclined to get them. But I'd prioritize the Void Engineers, with the Syndicate coming in a close second, followed by the NWO. The Progenitors would be a distant fourth, and Iteration X (which came out a decade earlier, just as the original World of Darkness was closing up shop) dead last \u2014 although its Hardsuits and the general shift away from them being cyborg warriors to being mechanical geniuses set the course for the revisions that the rest of the books underwent. <br /> <br /> But no, nothing about sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-29-2022, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T05:48:41-07:00","id":1491749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491746#post1491746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But no, nothing about sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so not worth getting, then.<br /> <br /> Seriously though. The Iteration X one was rather lacklustre and uninspired, so I never really was too keen on the rest, but the way you're presenting them, they sound like a lot of tun. I think I'll look into it!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T09:25:24-07:00","id":1491774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491673#post1491673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> I have this feeling that you're so caught up in trying to prove how well read you are that you've missed the forest for the trees. You can keep whatever views you want as long as you don't hurt anyone else by practising them, which you've already spoken at length about in the earlier discussion of the moral burden of the Mage. The problem is that you espoused a set of views that focused on a reductionist eurocentric view that neither gelled with the spirit of scientific achievement nor with the fact that the contributions and history of science are varied and quite more broad then presented. The whole marriage of God with the Scientific Method did not help (because face it, you know that Deism is but a waypoint on the road to the Scientific Method). You probably didn't mean it like it sounded, but it ended up interpreted like that.<br /> <br /> After all, we don't know how differently history would have unfolded with slightly different geopolitical and societal pressures. Europe happened to be in a place where it was rich, driven by a need for advancement and a lack of scruples about using it. Considering that history is just one set of variables and you being unable to experimentally prove that the same results couldn't be reproduced with a different set of variables, you may have to settle on the fact that there could have been other way for things to unfold and still end similar to where we are now.<br /> <br /> Now that we've gone through what antagonised a part of the forum, would you kindly get back to the topic? If you want to discuss the impacts of anarcho-capitalism in Mage and which paradigms and factions would support it, that's a solid topic. But let's stop this logorhoea under this topic as you're not going to change minds like this. At the end of the day people will pick their own reality and live with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just real quickly, Im not trying to preach my own political views here. I merely defended myself from unjust accusations based on the superficial labels. Im not discursing about what Anarcho Capitalism is, and Im not trying to gather followers. Like I said in fact, anyone is welcomed to criticize it at will - althought here is neither the place nor the time - but I do NOT admit being called, or being implied to be, something that I am not. That's all there is to it.<br /> <br /> Im not being eurocentric about nothing. The historical phenomena know as the &quot;Scientific Revolution&quot; happened in Europe. That's a fact that cannot be changed due to conviniences. This doesnt mean I am spouting any sort of &quot;Ubersmench&quot; nonsense, Im simply spouting in a historical fact. Just like it is a fact that while Europe were under the so called &quot;Dark Ages&quot; of superstitons and obscurantism, the Middle East was living its Golden Age.<br /> <br /> The Scientific Revolution was not something born out of the blue overnight. It's the culmination of a process that went brewing for thousands of years, ever since the Mesopotamians, and that took developments from Beijing to Lisbon, spamming ideas from the entirety of the Eurasia, exchanged by trade or by conquest.<br /> <br /> So, you continue to say that I disregard anything non european or anything that was done before the Scientific Revolution, but that's not something I ever said - at all. This revolution would never happened without the laid foundations that were built by greeks, etruscans, romans, carthagians, egyptians, babylonians, phoenicians, sumerians, persians, indians, chinese, arabs. All of those and many many more were essential for that final point, and without with it wouldnt have happened.<br /> <br /> Could it have happened in other place in another time? Sure it could. It could have happened in modern Iraq under the Abbasids in the 11th century, it could've happened in China in the 14th century. That could've had taken place in many different places of the globe.<br /> <br /> But it didnt. And there are several good reasons for why it happened so. And while it's too reductionist to set any of cause to a single variable, christian doctrine at the time was indeed one of the many causes for that. <br /> <br /> Why is it so scandalous to say that the cultural background of a population (you know, religion is part of the culture of a population, and a very important factor) is responsible for the societal evolution of that same population? I really dont understand what's up with all the uproar with such an innocuous declaration.<br /> <br /> Also, my point was 2 fold: first, the &quot;Technocratic Paradigm&quot; begins in Europe because that's were the &quot;Scientific Revolution&quot; began, and this is marked by the formalization of the Scientific Method as the tool for scientific inquiry (which once again you misunderstood me claiming that &quot;science aint all&quot;, which I also never claimed, thus I had to reinforce what I already had said by explaining that the Scientific Method itself is rooted in Philosophy and cant prove itself).<br /> <br /> And my second point was that the assumptions on the game Mage the Ascension were wrong, because the Technocratic Paradigm has NEVER become dominant or mainstream ANYWHERE, and that the fact is that in the real world atheism and materialism are fringe, minority ideas. And that the setting of MtA dont make sense: in the real world, scientific knowledge pushes belief towards materialism (to a certain degree), but in Mage, belief comes first, so you'd have to convince people of materialistic ideas BEFORE the &quot;materialistic reality&quot; could settle in, but that could never reflect the real world because Materialism is absolutely NOT the prevailing &quot;Consensus&quot; (of the real world). Therefore, MtA cannot be a reflection of our world, because it's based on false assumptions.<br /> <br /> Now, please explain it to me, why is any that Im saying causing such a scandalous reaction on everybody? Because I really cant understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490481-sex-and-the-technocracy?p=1491687#post1491687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really sure what you were expecting when you asked us to get back on topic in a topic whose original question was already answered. There is nothing else that can be said beyond redundant confirmation that 'yep, this is what Technocracy Reloaded says about gender identity and interpersonal relationships'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The original questions were already answered in full and to the maximum possible satisfaction. Which is why things began to drift towards technocratic broader worldview and philosophies, as an expansion on the original considerations. This thread however is basically finished by now, and only kep